					<description>Status: Offline
Operator: Genel Energy (operator, historically ~44% — exit terms agreed with the KRG January 2025); historic partners Sinopec/Addax ~36%, KRG ~20%
Role: Onshore field near Taq Taq, Kurdistan Region — PSC signed 2002; once the largest internationally operated field in Kurdistan
Capacity: Peaked at 116,000 b/d in 2015; fell on geological complications and reserve downgrades to under 5,000 b/d before the 2023 pipeline closure, then to zero — no production in 2024
Recent: Genel&apos;s exit sheds residual decommissioning liability, leaving it a 25% non-operated stake in Tawke; no confirmed operator or restart plan
Risks: No restart plan; reserve downgrades; Kurdistan payment and export uncertainty</description>
