				<Placemark id="07C24C13813F39F143AC">
					<name>Tawke oil field</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Operator: DNO ASA 75% (operator); Genel Energy 25%
Role: Tawke + Peshkabir complex, Kurdistan Region; gas capture and reinjection at Peshkabir roughly halves its emissions intensity; feeds the KRG export line at Fishkhabur
Capacity: 2025 average ~70,100 boe/d, ~77,300 by Q4; target 100,000 boe/d (2019–20 ran 100,000–120,000)
Recent: Ramp-up resumed February 2026 after a 30-month drilling hiatus (two rigs, eight wells, $100m Kurdistan capex vs $22m in 2025); production was shut as a precaution on 13 March 2026 amid the regional war, after damaging drone strikes in July 2025 — KRG pipeline flows resumed 18 March, and volatility remains the field&apos;s defining feature
Risks: Drone strikes (installations hit three times in 2025); war-related shutdowns; payment mechanism; licence renewal options to 2031/2036</description>
