					<name>Shaikan oil filed</name>
					<description>Status: Offline
Operator: Gulf Keystone Petroleum 80% (operator); MOL Group 20%
Role: Onshore field ~60 km north-west of Erbil, Kurdistan Region, producing since 2013
Capacity: ~60,000 b/d processing capacity across two facilities; 2P reserves 416 million bbl (Dec 2025), ~27 years of life; averaged ~41,560 b/d in 2025
Recent: Suspended late July 2026 — a precautionary shutdown amid the regional conflict, the second shut-in of the year (also halted February 2026); ~$269m revenue on 9.6 million bbl in the first eight months of 2025
Risks: Sole export route via the Iraq–Türkiye system, no redundancy; recurring conflict shutdowns; Baghdad–Erbil payment disputes; the US troop withdrawal from Kurdistan by 30 Sept 2026 removes an implicit security backstop</description>
