					<description>Status: Planned
Operator: Midland Oil Company with EBS Petroleum (China&apos;s ZhenHua Oil); Iraqi Drilling Company handling wells
Role: A super-giant field literally underlying eastern Baghdad — 11 km × 64 km; historically stranded by its urban location
Capacity: Reserves revised up to ~15 billion bbl — central Iraq&apos;s largest resource; near-term target 120,000 b/d of oil plus 25–50 MMcf/d of gas; 2009-era estimates saw up to 400,000 b/d potential
Recent: 18 wells being drilled; first oil targeted June 2026 and first gas September 2026 — startup not yet confirmed; the contract area was expanded in February 2025 (+~710 million bbl of estimated resources)
Risks: Urban drilling constraints; startup risk; Iraqi contractual terms; security</description>
