				<Placemark>
					<name>Cold Lake Blend Production Facility</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Operator: Imperial Oil (100% owner-operator)
Role: In-situ oil-sands complex, Cold Lake, Alberta — bitumen from the Clearwater formation across multiple pads; produces Cold Lake Blend, moved via the Cold Lake Pipeline to Edmonton/Hardisty
Capacity: ~190,000 b/d design; ~150,000 current, targeting 165,000 by 2030
Recent: Transition from cyclic steam to solvent-assisted SAGD — Grand Rapids onstream 2024, Leming steaming since summer 2025 (first oil end-2025), Mahihkan targeted 2029; the projects should add ~50,000 b/d by 2030 while cutting the steam-oil ratio from 4.4 toward 3.5
Risks: Natural-gas price exposure (steam generation); heavy-crude discount to WTI; execution risk converting old CSS infrastructure; Canadian emissions cap and carbon pricing</description>
