					<name>Ras Shukier oil field</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Operator: GUPCO (BP–EGPC 50/50); the small adjacent Shukheir Marine concession is run separately
Role: Field and Egypt&apos;s key Gulf of Suez export hub — the terminal aggregates crude from the GUPCO-area fields (incl. Morgan, discovered 1967) and feeds the 340 km Ras Shukeir–Asyut pipeline to inland refineries
Capacity: GUPCO&apos;s Gulf of Suez output ~71,250 b/d per a 2026 report (highest since 2019); field-specific figures are not published
Recent: The concession was extended in 2005 for 20 years (~through 2025) after $1.4bn of investment; no site-specific 2025–26 update found
Risks: Deep basin maturity and natural decline; concession renewal; Red Sea logistics exposure</description>
