					<description>Status: Operational
Operator: Suez Oil Company (SUCO) — EGPC with the ex-Wintershall Dea stake now held by Harbour Energy (2024)
Role: Coastal Gulf of Suez field ~80 km north of Hurghada with its own export terminal; produces from a fractured basement reservoir
Capacity: Small and mature — ~5,000 b/d from 19 wells on artificial lift and secondary recovery; ~80% of accessible resources already produced by the mid-2010s
Recent: Ownership moved to Harbour Energy in the 2024 $11.2bn Wintershall Dea acquisition
Risks: Deep depletion; lifting costs on a late-life asset</description>
