				<name>Offshore fields &amp; FPSOs</name>
				<Placemark>
					<name>Neptun Deep (Offshore Black Sea)</name>
					<description>Status: Planned
Operator: OMV Petrom and Romgaz, 50/50 — final investment decision 2023, first production targeted 2027
Role: The EU&apos;s largest natural gas project — a deep-water Black Sea development ~160 km offshore; gas rather than oil, mapped here because it will remake Romania&apos;s whole energy position
Capacity: ~100 Mt of gas over its life, enough to make Romania the EU&apos;s largest gas producer
Recent: Development drilling and subsea construction under way in a sea patrolled for drifting mines — the first major European offshore project built inside a war&apos;s insurance zone
Strategic role: The future counterweight to everything else on the Romanian map — a declining oil province funding its successor
Risks: War-zone construction and insurance; project execution offshore; gas-price cycles at start-up</description>
					<styleUrl>#msn_target</styleUrl>
