				<Placemark>
					<name>Khafji Oil Field (Partitioned Zone, Offshore)</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Operator: Al-Khafji Joint Operations — KGOC with Aramco Gulf Operations; output shared 50/50
Role: The offshore half of the Partitioned Zone — shallow-water heavy crude loaded at the Ras al-Khafji terminal on the shared coast
Capacity: ~300,000 b/d design within the PZ&apos;s ~500,000 combined; ramped back since the 2020 restart
Recent: Shut May 2015–February 2020 in the same bilateral dispute as Wafra (with an environmental-permit trigger on the Saudi side); its restart added real barrels to a tight market — and its 2026 liftings sit inside the closed strait like everything else in the northern Gulf
Strategic role: The maritime expression of the condominium — a field whose production schedule is written in two capitals
Risks: Bilateral alignment; in-Gulf loading under Hormuz closure; offshore drone and naval exposure; heavy-grade demand</description>
