				<Placemark>
					<name>Khor al-Amaya Oil Terminal (KAAOT)</name>
					<description>Status: Offline
Owner/Operator: Basra Oil Company / Iraqi Oil Ministry
Role: Iraq&apos;s second offshore loading platform, a few kilometres from ABOT — historically a twin export terminal, largely idle for years after war damage, tanker collisions and chronic underinvestment
Capacity: Nominal berths largely out of service; periodic rehabilitation plans announced without sustained restoration
Connectivity: Same Fao-fed subsea system as ABOT
Recent: Rehabilitation repeatedly studied as part of Iraq&apos;s export-capacity ambitions; the 2026 crisis made its idle berths a visible cost — a second terminal that could not relieve the first
Strategic role: The spare capacity Iraq doesn&apos;t have — the physical difference between nominal and usable export infrastructure
Risks: Structural degradation; funding priority against onshore projects; the same Hormuz dependence as everything else in the south</description>
