					<description>Status: Operational
Operator: ADNOC Offshore — ADNOC 60%, ExxonMobil 28%, INPEX/JODCO 12%
Role: The world&apos;s second-largest offshore oil field — developed from four artificial drilling islands with extended-reach wells replacing dozens of conventional platforms
Capacity: ~1 million b/d achieved, with expansion targeted toward 1.2 million b/d; the Upper Zakum export grade
Connectivity: Subsea lines to Zirku Island for processing, storage and export — loading remains inside the Persian Gulf
Recent: 2026 — the in-Gulf loading point left this barrel Hormuz-exposed even as the UAE ran at 82% of export rates overall; the contrast with pipeline-served onshore Murban is the emirate&apos;s core supply-security lesson
Risks: In-Gulf export dependence; island drilling-centre concentration; partner-alignment on expansion pace</description>
