					<name>Zuluf Oil Field (Offshore)</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Operator: Saudi Aramco
Role: One of the kingdom&apos;s giant offshore fields, ~240 km northwest of Dhahran in the shallow Gulf; producing Arabian Medium/Heavy since the 1970s
Capacity: ~800,000–825,000 b/d maximum sustained capacity; the Zuluf increment programme adds ~600,000 b/d of Arabian Heavy via a new central processing facility — the largest single project in Aramco&apos;s offshore maintain-potential effort, targeted around 2026
Connectivity: Offshore gathering platforms to onshore processing and the east-coast export system
Recent: Expansion execution through the 2026 period even as exports ran constrained by the Hormuz closure
Risks: Offshore infrastructure within regional drone/naval reach; project execution at scale; heavy-grade demand cycles</description>
