					<description>Status: Operational
Operator: Saudi Aramco
Role: Offshore giant in the northern Gulf near the Zuluf–Safaniya cluster; Arabian Medium; discovered 1967
Capacity: ~500,000 b/d, rising toward ~800,000 with the Marjan increment (+300,000 b/d) — new offshore platforms, GOSP-4 and major gas/NGL processing at the Tanajib onshore complex; phased start-up from ~2025
Connectivity: Offshore gathering to Tanajib and the east-coast processing and export chain
Recent: One of the two flagship offshore expansions (with Zuluf) sustaining Saudi maximum capacity as older increments decline
Risks: Mega-project execution; offshore exposure in the northern Gulf, the closest Saudi production to Iranian waters; processing concentration at Tanajib</description>
