					<description>Status: Operational
Operator: Saudi Aramco
Role: The world&apos;s largest offshore oil field — shallow-water Persian Gulf, ~265 km north of Dhahran, producing since 1957; the backbone of the Arabian Heavy export grade
Capacity: ~1.3 million b/d maximum sustained capacity; a long-term expansion programme (jackets, platforms, tie-ins) is part of Aramco&apos;s offshore maintain-potential effort
Connectivity: Offshore gathering to onshore processing, then the Ras Tanura export system
Recent: 2026 — heavy-grade exports constrained by the Hormuz closure; offshore infrastructure inside the Gulf cannot reroute west without passing onshore processing first
Risks: Offshore facilities within range of regional drones and naval incidents; heavy-crude demand cycles; ageing shallow-water infrastructure</description>
