				<Placemark>
					<name>ISAB Refinery – Priolo Gargallo</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Owner: ISAB — GOI Energy (Cyprus) with Trafigura supply and offtake agreements; Ludoil Capital signed in May 2026 to acquire 51% and return the plant to Italian ownership, pending Golden Power approval
Capacity: 320,000 b/d — Italy&apos;s largest refining complex (~20% of national capacity), three interconnected production sites across Priolo, Augusta and Melilli, with a 540 MW cogeneration plant
Feedstock: Mediterranean cargo market — the crude slate rebuilt from scratch after losing Urals in the 2022 embargo
Main products: Gasoline, diesel, jet, fuel oil, petrochemical feedstocks for the Priolo cluster
Markets: Italy (about a quarter of its petrol) and Mediterranean cargo trade
Recent: The most owned refinery in Europe — Lukoil until the embargo, trusteeship, GOI/Trafigura from 2023, court-supervised crisis negotiations exited February 2026, the Ludoil deal signed May 2026; declared of national strategic interest by decree
Strategic role: The physical anchor of the CIF Augusta pricing zone — and the market&apos;s live case study in what sanctions do to a merchant refinery&apos;s ownership, feedstock and finances at once
Risks: Ownership-transition execution; merchant-refinery margin exposure; the cluster&apos;s future if any transition stalls</description>
					<styleUrl>#msn_volcano1</styleUrl>
