				<Placemark>
					<name>SATORP Jubail Refinery</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Owner: Saudi Aramco 62.5%, TotalEnergies 37.5%
Capacity: ~460,000 b/d — one of the world&apos;s most complex full-conversion refineries, built to run Arabian Heavy
Feedstock: Arabian Heavy crude from the eastern system
Main products: Ultra-low-sulphur diesel and gasoline, jet fuel, LPG, petcoke, paraxylene, benzene
Markets: Export-oriented toward Asia and Europe, plus domestic supply
Recent: The $11bn Amiral expansion under construction — a mixed-feed cracker integrating the refinery into one of the region&apos;s largest petrochemical complexes, start-up targeted 2027
Strategic role: The model Aramco downstream JV — heavy crude in, premium products and chemicals out, on the Gulf coast
Risks: Hormuz dependence for exports; construction execution; petrochemical margin cycles</description>
					<styleUrl>#msn_volcano3</styleUrl>
