				<Placemark>
					<name>SASREF Jubail Refinery</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Owner: Saudi Aramco (100% since buying out Shell&apos;s 50% in 2019)
Capacity: ~305,000 b/d
Feedstock: Arabian Light from the eastern system
Main products: Diesel, jet/kerosene, naphtha, LPG, fuel oil, sulphur
Markets: Export-focused with domestic supply obligations
Recent: Integration deepened into Aramco&apos;s wholly-owned refining system after the Shell exit; debottlenecking studies toward higher capacity
Strategic role: The older half of the Jubail refining pair — Aramco&apos;s proof it can run ex-JV assets alone
Risks: Hormuz dependence; competition from newer, more complex plants; ageing units</description>
					<styleUrl>#msn_volcano3</styleUrl>
