				<Placemark>
					<name>Jazan Refinery &amp; IGCC Complex</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Owner: Saudi Aramco
Capacity: ~400,000 b/d, integrated with one of the world&apos;s largest gasification/combined-cycle power complexes (IGCC) running on refinery residues
Feedstock: Arabian Heavy and Medium delivered by tanker to the adjacent terminal
Main products: Gasoline, ultra-low-sulphur diesel, jet fuel; power for the southern grid
Markets: Product exports via the Red Sea plus southern domestic supply
Recent: Ramped through the mid-2020s after phased commissioning; sits in the far south-west — inside the zone the Houthi campaign has made the Red Sea&apos;s most dangerous, and the July 2026 threat declaration against Saudi ports lands closest here
Strategic role: Aramco&apos;s southern outpost — a Red Sea export refinery deliberately far from the Gulf, now testing whether distance from Hormuz equals safety
Risks: Houthi missile/drone range; remote logistics; IGCC operational complexity</description>
