				<Placemark>
					<name>Petro Rabigh Refinery &amp; Petrochemical Complex</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Owner: Petro Rabigh — Saudi Aramco ~60% (raised in 2024 by acquiring half of Sumitomo Chemical&apos;s stake), Sumitomo Chemical retaining a reduced share
Capacity: ~400,000 b/d integrated with a large ethane/naphtha petrochemical complex on the Red Sea
Feedstock: Arabian crude delivered via the west-coast system, plus ethane
Main products: Gasoline, diesel, jet, fuel oil; ethylene and propylene derivatives, aromatics
Markets: Red Sea product exports and Asian petrochemical sales
Recent: Recapitalised and restructured in 2024 as Aramco took control — years of losses made it the problem child of the downstream portfolio
Strategic role: The Red Sea&apos;s integrated refining-petrochemical site, between Jeddah and Yanbu on the non-Hormuz coast
Risks: Chronic financial underperformance; petrochemical margins; Red Sea shipping insecurity</description>
