				<Placemark>
					<name>YASREF Yanbu Refinery</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Owner: Saudi Aramco 62.5%, Sinopec 37.5%
Capacity: ~400,000 b/d full-conversion, running Arabian Heavy
Main products: Ultra-low-sulphur diesel and gasoline, petcoke, sulphur — an export machine
Markets: Asia and Europe from the Yanbu terminals
Recent: The Chinese anchor in Saudi downstream — Sinopec&apos;s stake mirrors Aramco&apos;s push into Chinese refining; central to the 2026 westbound rerouting as Yanbu became the kingdom&apos;s working export gate
Strategic role: One-third of the Yanbu refining cluster (with SAMREF and the domestic Aramco plant) that turns Petroline crude into Red Sea product exports without touching Hormuz
Risks: Red Sea shipping insecurity and the July 2026 Houthi threat perimeter; heavy-crude conversion economics</description>
