				<Placemark>
					<name>SAMREF Yanbu Refinery</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Owner: Saudi Aramco Mobil Refinery — Aramco 50%, ExxonMobil 50%
Capacity: ~400,000 b/d
Feedstock: Arabian Light delivered by Petroline
Main products: Gasoline, diesel, jet, naphtha, LPG, fuel oil
Markets: Red Sea exports and western domestic supply
Recent: Clean-fuels upgrades completed in the 2020s; running as part of the Yanbu cluster that carried Saudi exports through the 2026 Hormuz closure
Strategic role: The veteran of the west-coast strategy — proof since the 1980s that Saudi barrels can reach the Atlantic basin without the strait
Risks: Red Sea insecurity; ageing units against newer competitors; JV alignment</description>
