				<Placemark>
					<name>OMV Schwechat refinery</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Owner: OMV (Austrian state ~31.5% via ÖBAG, ADNOC ~24.9%)
Capacity: ~9.6 Mt/yr (~200,000 b/d); integrated with Borealis polyolefins on site
Feedstock: Crude via the Adria-Wien Pipeline (AWP), a TAL branch from Trieste — no seaborne access; some Danube barge supply
Main products: Diesel, gasoline, jet fuel (Vienna Airport next door), heating oil, petrochemical feedstocks
Markets: Austria; Vienna Airport
Renewables: Co-processing of renewable feedstocks; sustainable-fuel capacity under development
Recent: June 2022 — a distillation column collapsed during a pressure test, idling much of the plant for months; Austria released strategic reserves. Back at full rates since
Strategic role: Austria&apos;s only refinery — a landlocked site entirely dependent on the Trieste/TAL corridor, the Austrian twin of Bayernoil&apos;s supply logic
Risks: Single-corridor crude supply (TAL/AWP); 2022 incident history; Danube low water limits barge alternatives; European margins</description>
