				<Placemark>
					<name>Godorf refinery</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Owner: Shell Deutschland
Capacity: ~187,000 b/d — now the only crude unit of the Shell Energy &amp; Chemicals Park Rheinland (Wesseling&apos;s ~147,000 b/d distillation ended March 2025)
Feedstock: Seaborne crude from Rotterdam via the Rotterdam–Rhine Pipeline (RRP)
Main products: Diesel, gasoline, jet, heating oil, naphtha; vacuum gasoil piped to Wesseling&apos;s base-oil plant
Markets: North Rhine-Westphalia; naphtha to the LyondellBasell and INEOS crackers; products into the Rhine-Main pipeline (RMR), whose control centre sits at Godorf
Recent: 2025–26 — park reconfigured (crude only at Godorf); 10 MW electrolyser and biomethane plant on site; Godorf&apos;s Rhine berth cut off from ARA barges in the 2025 and 2026 low-water episodes
Strategic role: The last crude distillation in the Cologne cluster — anchor of naphtha supply to one of Europe&apos;s densest petrochemical zones, and the origin of the RMR
Risks: Cluster naphtha shortfall as regional refining shrinks (ICIS: −0.75 to −1 Mt/yr light naphtha); Rhine low water; European margins</description>
