				<Placemark id="0BAD6318AD3E92734D19">
					<name>Gazprom Neft Omsk Refinery</name>
					<description>Status: Reduced
Owner: Gazprom Neft
Capacity: ~22 Mt/yr (~440,000–460,000 b/d) — Russia&apos;s largest refinery
Feedstock: Russian crude via the domestic pipeline network
Main products: Gasoline, diesel, jet fuel, LPG, bitumen, petroleum coke, sulphur, petrochemical feedstocks
Markets: Siberia, the Urals and the Russian domestic market; some exports to neighbours
Recent: July 2026 — a Ukrainian drone attack damaged major crude-distillation units and temporarily halted operations. 2024 throughput ~22 Mt, yielding ~5 Mt gasoline and ~8 Mt diesel
Strategic role: Critical supplier of transport fuels to Siberia and the domestic market
Risks: Long-range drone attacks; fires; sanctions and equipment-replacement constraints; severe winters; pipeline disruption</description>
