				<Placemark id="0B015372A33EB40D5613">
					<name>S-OIL Onsan Refinery</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Owner: S-OIL Corporation (Saudi Aramco controlling shareholder)
Capacity: ~669,000 b/d across three crude units
Feedstock: Mainly imported Middle Eastern crude, especially Saudi grades, plus other light-to-sour crudes
Main products: Gasoline, diesel, jet, naphtha, LPG, marine fuels, base oils, paraxylene, petrochemical feedstocks
Markets: South Korea; exports to NE/SE Asia, Europe and the US
Recent: ~96% average crude-unit utilisation in 2025; maintenance of No. 2 CDU and No. 2 RFCC planned for 2026
Strategic role: Major residue-upgrading and paraxylene capacity — Aramco&apos;s Korean downstream anchor
Risks: Middle East crude dependence; Hormuz disruption; typhoons; outages; weak margins; petrochemical overcapacity</description>
