				<Placemark id="0EB6C96CCE3F337D9842">
					<name>Sinopec Zhenhai Refining &amp; Chemical Complex</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Owner: Sinopec Zhenhai Refining &amp; Chemical Company (Sinopec)
Capacity: ~40 Mt/yr (~800,000 b/d) across the integrated refining-chemical base — Sinopec&apos;s first 40 Mt/yr site
Feedstock: Imported Middle Eastern, Russian, African and other crudes, plus condensates and intermediates
Main products: Gasoline, diesel, jet, LPG, naphtha, aromatics, ethylene, plastics
Markets: Eastern China (Yangtze River Delta); some product and petrochemical exports across Asia
Recent: March 2026 — both steam crackers cut to ~70–80% utilisation amid Middle East supply disruption and weak petrochemical economics
Strategic role: One of China&apos;s largest integrated hubs, feeding the industrialised Yangtze Delta
Risks: Imported-crude dependence; Hormuz and Malacca disruption; Ningbo port congestion; typhoons; outages; weak margins; Chinese export restrictions</description>
