				<Placemark id="00E0A67AB93F337E4686">
					<name>PetroChina Dalian Petrochemical Refinery</name>
					<description>Status: Offline
Owner: PetroChina (CNPC)
Capacity: ~410,000 b/d (~20.5 Mt/yr) historical
Feedstock: Historically Russian ESPO crude and other imported/domestic grades
Main products: Gasoline, diesel, jet, naphtha, LPG, marine fuels, petrochemical feedstocks
Markets: North-east China; regional Asia via Dalian&apos;s port
Recent: Shut in 2025 under a relocation/modernisation plan. A 2026 restart of one 200,000 b/d crude unit to run discounted Russian oil was considered, then delayed. Replacement: a new ~200,000 b/d refinery plus a large ethylene unit approved on Changxing Island
Strategic role: Historically one of northern China&apos;s largest refineries and a key processor of Russian Far East crude
Risks: Permanent closure or delayed restart; regulatory uncertainty; sanctions on Russian crude; weak Chinese demand; overcapacity</description>
