				<Placemark>
					<name>Sonatrach Skikda Refinery &amp; Petrochemical Complex</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Owner: Sonatrach
Capacity: ~16.5 Mt/yr (~320,000–335,000 b/d) — Algeria&apos;s largest refinery; commissioned 1980, major rehabilitation ~2013
Feedstock: Algerian crude, mainly light Saharan grades via the national pipeline network
Main products: Gasoline, diesel, jet, LPG, naphtha, fuel oil, bitumen, aromatics (benzene, xylene)
Markets: Algerian domestic market; exports to Europe and the Mediterranean via the adjacent Skikda port
Recent: Additional fuel-oil conversion and hydrocracking capacity under development to raise gasoline/diesel yields
Strategic role: One of Africa&apos;s largest refining sites, supplying a large share of national demand
Risks: Unit outages and fires; ageing infrastructure; pipeline interruption; Mediterranean shipping; project delays</description>
