				<Placemark>
					<name>RAPID Refinery</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Owner: PRefChem — formerly a 50:50 Petronas–Saudi Aramco JV; on 25 May 2026 the partners agreed to transfer Aramco&apos;s stake to Petronas, making it wholly Petronas-owned
Capacity: 300,000 b/d crude distillation (~9 Mt/yr of products); ARDS, two gasoline units, hydrocrackers, hydrogen plant
Feedstock: Imported crude — historically Aramco term barrels and Petronas supply — via the Pengerang deepwater terminal
Main products: Euro 4/5 gasoline and diesel, jet, LPG, naphtha and streams to the adjacent petrochemical complex
Markets: Malaysia and SE Asia; Asia-Pacific exports; competes directly with Singapore&apos;s Jurong hub
Recent: A gasoline unit down Jan–May 2025 and again Feb–April 2026, cutting crude runs; full commercial operation reached only in 2022 after a 2019 fire and 2020 explosion; Aramco&apos;s exit removes its guaranteed crude supply
Strategic role: Malaysia&apos;s largest refinery and anchor of its flagship downstream project
Risks: Repeated outages and reliability issues; loss of Aramco offtake certainty; Asian margin volatility and new competing capacity; 100% imported crude; process-safety history</description>
