				<Placemark id="0E467C7C173FCEB24E88">
					<name>VAROPreem Lysekil Refinery &amp; Renewable Fuels Hub</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Renewables: Dedicated unit — up to 900,000 m³/yr from the upgraded Synsat unit; total Lysekil renewable capacity &gt;1 million m³/yr
Owner: VAROPreem
Capacity: ~220,000 b/d conventional — Scandinavia&apos;s largest refinery
Feedstock: Imported crude via the Brofjorden deep-water terminal, plus renewable feeds (tall oil, used cooking oils, animal fats, pyrolysis oils)
Main products: Diesel, gasoline, LPG, HVO renewable diesel and co-processed renewable fuels
Markets: Sweden, Norway and NW Europe
Recent: Synsat upgrade in service since 2025 — up to 40% renewable material co-processed with diesel
Strategic role: Major Nordic refinery and large-scale renewable-fuels hub supporting road, marine, aviation and industrial decarbonisation
Risks: Seaborne-feedstock dependence; outages; North Sea weather; energy and carbon costs; uncertainty over future fuel demand</description>
