				<Placemark>
					<name>ENEOS Kawasaki Refinery</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Owner: ENEOS (Japan&apos;s largest refiner)
Capacity: ~247,000–249,000 b/d — ENEOS&apos;s largest refinery and the biggest on Tokyo Bay, with Japan&apos;s largest fluid catalytic cracker
Feedstock: Imported crude via Kawasaki&apos;s coastal industrial zone, backed by abundant sea and land transport
Main products: Gasoline, kerosene, jet, diesel; petrochemicals — two ethylene crackers (540,000 + 448,000 t/yr) supplying neighbouring plants by pipeline
Markets: The Tokyo metropolitan area, Japan&apos;s largest consumption centre
Recent: Feb 2025 — ENEOS announced the Ukishima South cracker (448,000 t/yr) will close by end-FY2027, citing Chinese overcapacity; group targets 90% refinery utilisation by FY2027, up from 78% in 2024
Strategic role: The volume anchor of Tokyo&apos;s fuel supply — refining and petrochemicals integrated in one coastal plant
Risks: Earthquake exposure; petrochemical margin weakness; demand decline; urban-industrial interface</description>
