				<Placemark>
					<name>Showa Yokkaichi Sekiyu – Yokkaichi Refinery</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Owner: Showa Yokkaichi Sekiyu Co. — Idemitsu group since the Showa Shell merger (April 2019), with Mitsubishi and others as minority holders
Capacity: 255,000 b/d — the largest refinery in the Idemitsu group and the second-largest in Japan; in operation since 1958; residue FCC (55,000 b/d) plus FCC give it solid heavy-oil conversion
Feedstock: Middle Eastern crude delivered by VLCC — the Aramco supply relationship is a Showa Shell inheritance
Main products: Gasoline, kerosene, jet, diesel, heavy fuel oils, LPG, petrochemical feedstocks
Markets: Central Japan (Chubu) and the wider Idemitsu supply network
Recent: Feb 2026 — Idemitsu reversed refinery-closure plans, keeping its six-refinery network until at least 2030 as EV adoption stalls
Strategic role: The volume anchor of the Ise Bay refining cluster — and a landmark of environmental history: the 1960s Yokkaichi asthma litigation against the complex&apos;s operators shaped Japanese pollution law
Risks: Earthquake and typhoon exposure; Japan&apos;s structural demand decline; single-site scale concentration</description>
