					<name>Tüpraş Kırıkkale Refinery</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Owner: Tüpraş (Koç Holding) — Turkey&apos;s dominant refiner
Capacity: ~110,000–115,000 b/d, serving Ankara and central Anatolia
Feedstock: Imported and Iraqi-origin crude delivered by the Ceyhan–Kırıkkale pipeline
Main products: Gasoline, diesel, jet fuel, LPG, heating oil, bitumen for the inland market
Markets: Central Anatolia — the plant that bailed out the Mediterranean coast when ATAŞ stopped refining in 2004, trucking fuel 485 km south
Strategic role: Turkey&apos;s only inland refinery — the demand anchor that justifies Ceyhan&apos;s one landward pipeline
Risks: Single-pipeline feedstock dependence; inland location without marine fallback; competition from seaborne products via Mersin</description>
