					<name>OQ8 Duqm Refinery</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Owner: OQ8 — OQ and Kuwait Petroleum International, 50/50
Capacity: 255,000 b/d (raised from the 230,000 design in 2025) — the region&apos;s newest export refinery, onstream 2023–24 in the Duqm Special Economic Zone on the Arabian Sea
Feedstock: Designed for a Kuwaiti-Omani crude diet (~65% Kuwait Export Crude, ~35% Omani) — the Kuwaiti half arrives by tanker through Hormuz, the strategic irony of an outside-the-strait refinery
Main products: Diesel, jet fuel, naphtha, LPG — middle-distillate-weighted for export
Markets: Asia, East Africa and Europe from the adjacent Port of Duqm
Recent: 2026 — its open-ocean location made it one of the few Gulf-region refineries whose product exports faced no chokepoint at all; feedstock flexibility tested as Kuwaiti deliveries navigated the closure
Strategic role: Kuwait&apos;s outside-Hormuz insurance and Oman&apos;s industrial bet, in one plant
Risks: Feedstock supply chain through the strait; remote-location logistics; ramp-up economics</description>
