					<name>KAR Refinery – Khabat (Erbil)</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Owner: KAR Group — the private conglomerate that also built and operates the KRG export pipeline
Capacity: ~200,000 b/d nameplate across phased expansions — the Kurdistan Region&apos;s largest refinery; actual throughput varies with crude availability
Feedstock: Kurdistan crude, notably from the KAR-operated Khurmala Dome — the same barrels that sell domestically at ~$31 when export economics collapse
Main products: Gasoline, diesel, kerosene, jet fuel, LPG, fuel oil for the KRI market
Markets: Erbil and the Kurdistan Region — with Lanaz and Baizan, the refining base that turns pipeline politics into local fuel security
Recent: KRI energy infrastructure entered the drone-attack era in 2025 (Tawke and other fields struck repeatedly); the refinery benefits whenever export disputes trap cheap crude at home
Strategic role: The industrial anchor of KAR&apos;s vertical system — dome, pipeline, refinery — and the reason Kurdistan rides out export shutdowns better than Baghdad expects
Risks: Drone and rocket exposure; dependence on KRI crude allocation politics; single-owner concentration across the whole chain</description>
