					<name>ExxonMobil Rotterdam Refinery</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Owner: ExxonMobil (Esso Nederland B.V.)
Capacity: ~190,000 b/d
Feedstock: Wide slate, light sweet to heavy sour, by ship to the Maasvlakte and Europoort tank farms then by pipeline to the refinery
Main products: LPG, naphtha, kerosene, diesel, sulphur, petcoke, chemical feedstocks, Group II/II+ base oils
Markets: Netherlands and NW European fuel, lubricant and petrochemical markets
Recent: ExxonMobil paused a European chemical-recycling investment (incl. Rotterdam) in 2025 over EU recycled-content rules
Strategic role: Integrated refinery-aromatics-hydrogen complex; the 2019 hydrocracker upgrade made it Europe&apos;s only world-scale Group II/II+ producer
Risks: Rhine and port logistics; outages; energy and carbon costs; regulatory uncertainty; margins</description>
