					<name>Kulevi Oil Refinery</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Owner: Black Sea Petroleum LLC — beneficial owners reported as Maka Asatiani and Konstantin Gogelia, with Dunamis LLC (29.34%) and Georgian bank/state financing
Capacity: Phase 1 ~1.1 Mt/yr (~22,000 b/d); Phase 2 planned to ~2.9–3.5 Mt/yr by 2026–27
Feedstock: Crude via the adjacent SOCAR Kulevi terminal — including, per EU and investigative reporting, Russian-origin crude
Main products: Diesel, gasoline and other products
Markets: Georgia and regional export
Recent: Operations started ~2025; named in the EU&apos;s 21st sanctions package (23 July 2026) for processing Russian crude, with a six-month grace period; operator says Russian processing stops by Aug–Sept 2026. TI Georgia and OCCRP allege sanctions-evasion links (Mikhail Gutseriev; the sanctioned tanker Kayseri, Oct 2025)
Strategic role: Georgia&apos;s first and only refinery — a Black Sea processing hub for Caspian and, per sanctions findings, Russian crude
Risks: Sanctions exposure; reputational and legal risk; ownership opacity; dependence on the adjacent terminal</description>
