				<Placemark id="01AF5FA0193FCEBB0A64">
					<name>VAROPreem Gothenburg Refinery &amp; Renewable Fuels Hub</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Renewables: Dedicated unit — ~300,000–320,000 m³/yr incl. HVO100; the converted hydroprocessing unit can run 100% renewable feedstock
Owner: VAROPreem
Capacity: ~132,000 b/d total refining capacity
Feedstock: Imported crude plus renewable feeds — tall oil, used cooking oils, animal fats, industrial and food-sector by-products
Main products: Diesel, gasoline, LPG, HVO100 renewable diesel and co-processed renewable fuels
Markets: Sweden and NW Europe, incl. HVO100 exports to the Netherlands
Recent: ~900,000 litres/day of renewable fuel
Strategic role: One of Sweden&apos;s principal renewable-fuels hubs and a European co-processing pioneer (since 2010)
Risks: Seaborne crude and feedstock dependence; outages; port disruption; feedstock-price volatility; sustainability rules; European fuel policy</description>
