				<Placemark>
					<name>Fuji Oil Sodegaura Refinery</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Owner: Fuji Oil Company — controlled by Idemitsu Kosan since October 2025 (tender offer completed, delisting planned)
Capacity: 143,000 b/d — the company&apos;s only refinery, in operation since 1968
Feedstock: Imported crude, Kuwaiti grades prominent, via the refinery&apos;s own Tokyo Bay pier
Main products: Gasoline, kerosene, diesel, heavy fuel oil, LPG, aromatics (benzene, mixed xylenes)
Markets: Tokyo metropolitan area; petrochemical feedstocks by pipeline to the adjacent Sumitomo Chemical Chiba Works; export capability
Recent: October 2025 — Idemitsu acquired control (~53% for ¥19.6bn), folding a seventh site into its network
Strategic role: A small, deep-conversion niche player — its Eureka vacuum-residue thermal cracker is the only unit of its kind, turning heavy crude into light products and aromatics
Risks: Single-refinery company; earthquake exposure (2021 quake shutdown); Japan&apos;s structural demand decline; integration under new ownership</description>
