				<Placemark>
					<name>Osaka International Refining Chiba Refinery</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Owner: Osaka International Refining Company — ENEOS 51%, PetroChina International (Japan) 49%; the JV kept its &quot;Osaka&quot; name when it moved here in December 2020 after the Osaka refinery closed
Capacity: 129,000 b/d; started 1968 as Kyokuto Petroleum Industries, later Tonen General, then ENEOS
Feedstock: Crude procured by PetroChina; residue FCC and hydrocracking units
Main products: Gasoline, kerosene, jet, diesel, petrochemical feedstocks for the Keiyo industrial complex
Markets: Export-oriented — PetroChina markets the output, mainly to East Asia; also the Kanto region, Japan&apos;s largest demand centre
Recent: Pipeline-integrated with the neighbouring Cosmo Chiba refinery since 2018 (Keiyo Seisei JV)
Strategic role: China&apos;s only refining foothold in Japan — a Japanese refinery running on Chinese-procured crude for Chinese-marketed exports
Risks: JV-renewal and geopolitical exposure; export-margin dependence; earthquake shutdowns (2022 quake power outage)</description>
