				<Placemark>
					<name>Cosmo Oil Chiba Refinery</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Owner: Cosmo Oil (Cosmo Energy Holdings) — Japan&apos;s third-largest refiner
Capacity: 177,000 b/d across two crude units; Nelson Complexity ~10.2; operating since 1963
Feedstock: Middle East-weighted imports — UAE, Saudi Arabia, Qatar, Kuwait — plus other grades
Main products: Gasoline, kerosene, jet, diesel, heavy fuel oil, naphtha, LPG
Markets: Tokyo metropolitan area and the Keiyo industrial complex
Recent: Nov 2024 — CCS feasibility study awarded to Chiyoda under Japan&apos;s advanced-CCS programme, targeting capture at the refinery; pipeline-linked to the OIRC/ENEOS Chiba refinery since 2018
Strategic role: One of the three Ichihara refineries that make Chiba Japan&apos;s densest refining zone
Risks: Earthquake and tsunami exposure — the 2011 quake destroyed the LPG tank farm in fires and explosions, a landmark process-safety case; demand decline; ageing units</description>
