				<Placemark>
					<name>TOA Oil Keihin Refinery</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Owner: Toa Oil Co. — wholly owned by Idemitsu Kosan since September 2022 (came with the Showa Shell merger; minorities bought out for ~¥19.5bn)
Capacity: 70,000 b/d — the smallest Tokyo Bay refinery, at Mizue in Kawasaki
Feedstock: Imported crude and heavy feedstocks; vacuum distillation and coking give it a heavy-oil cracking profile
Main products: Gasoline, kerosene, diesel, fuel oil; electricity — power generation is a second business line on site
Markets: Tokyo metropolitan area, within the Idemitsu supply network
Recent: Feb 2026 — Idemitsu&apos;s reversal of refinery-closure plans keeps its six-refinery network, Keihin included, running until at least 2030
Strategic role: A small conversion refinery whose survival tracks the pace of Japan&apos;s EV transition — the marginal plant in the marginal market
Risks: Smallest-scale economics; closure risk if demand or policy shifts again; fire history (Dec 2019 full shutdown); earthquake exposure</description>
