				<Placemark>
					<name>Idemitsu Kosan Chiba Complex</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Owner: Idemitsu Kosan
Capacity: ~190,000–195,000 b/d — the largest plant in the Idemitsu group, refining ~10 million kL of crude a year
Feedstock: Crude unloaded at the Keiyo Sea Berth (two 300,000 t tankers) and pumped ashore by undersea pipeline at ~10,000 kL/hour
Main products: Gasoline, kerosene, jet, diesel, lubricants (a core national lube site), petrochemicals — refinery and chemical plant linked by 50 pipelines
Markets: Kanto region; ethylene chain into the Keiyo complex
Recent: The 374,000 t/yr ethylene cracker closes by March 2027 (Dec 2025 consolidation deal with Mitsui Chemicals); a waste-plastic recycled-oil unit under construction; a subsidised ~100,000 kL/yr SAF plant targeted for ~2028; Feb 2026 — Idemitsu reversed refinery-closure plans, keeping six refineries until 2030 as EV adoption stalls
Strategic role: Idemitsu&apos;s most important production, development and logistics base
Risks: Petrochemical overcapacity; demand decline; fires (July 2024 lube unit); earthquake exposure</description>
