				<Placemark>
					<name>ENEOS Sakai Refinery</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Owner: ENEOS (Japan&apos;s largest refiner)
Capacity: 141,000 b/d, on the Sakai waterfront of Osaka Bay
Feedstock: Imported crude, Middle East-weighted, via the refinery&apos;s marine berths
Main products: Gasoline, kerosene, jet, diesel, heavy fuel oil, LPG, petrochemical feedstocks
Markets: Osaka and the Kansai region — Japan&apos;s second-largest demand centre
Recent: Became ENEOS&apos;s only refinery in Kansai after the neighbouring Osaka refinery ceased refining in October 2020 (converted to an asphalt-fuelled power plant); the group targets 90% refinery utilisation by FY2027, up from 78% in 2024
Strategic role: The last ENEOS crude-processing site serving the Osaka conurbation — regional supply concentrated on one plant
Risks: Single-refinery exposure for ENEOS in Kansai; earthquake and typhoon exposure; Japan&apos;s structural demand decline</description>
