				<Placemark>
					<name>Cosmo Oil Sakai Refinery</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Owner: Cosmo Oil (Cosmo Energy Holdings)
Capacity: 100,000 b/d — the mid-sized plant of Cosmo&apos;s three-refinery system, on Osaka Bay
Feedstock: Middle Eastern crude — UAE and Saudi grades prominent across the Cosmo system; used cooking oil arrives by truck for the SAF plant
Main products: Gasoline, kerosene, jet, diesel, heavy fuel oil; neat SAF blended on site and shipped by sea from the refinery pier
Markets: Kansai region; SAF supplied to Kansai, Chubu and Haneda airports since April 2025 — customers include JAL, ANA, Delta, Finnair and DHL
Recent: Japan&apos;s first SAF mass-production unit (SAFFAIRE SKY ENERGY, ~30,000 kL/yr, JV with JGC and Revo) completed Dec 2024, first delivery April 2025; an April 2025 explosion at a sulphuric-acid unit and a Dec 2025 unplanned CDU outage left both the crude unit and SAF plant running; a JOGMEC-backed CCS study is also under way
Strategic role: The proof-of-concept site for Japan&apos;s 10%-SAF-by-2030 mandate — conventional refining and certified renewable jet on one fence line
Risks: Small scale; SAF economics (3–5× jet fuel cost, subsidy-dependent); UCO feedstock competition; earthquake exposure</description>
