				<Placemark>
					<name>PARCO Mid-Country Refininery</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Owner: Pak-Arab Refinery Limited — Government of Pakistan 60%, Emirate of Abu Dhabi 40% via Mubadala
Capacity: 120,000 b/d (upgraded from 100,000) — Pakistan&apos;s largest and most modern refinery, and the only mild-conversion plant of the country&apos;s five; commissioned 2000 at a cost of ~$886m
Feedstock: Imported light and medium crudes (historically ~60% Arabian Light, 40% Upper Zakum), pumped inland from Karachi via the Karachi–Mahmoodkot pipeline
Main products: Gasoline, Euro-compliant diesel (first DHDS in Pakistan), jet fuel, kerosene, LPG, furnace oil, bitumen, sulphur
Markets: Punjab and central Pakistan — products flow north via the Mahmoodkot–Faisalabad–Machike pipeline
Recent: A ~$600m clean-fuels (Euro-V) programme reported complete; a further upgrade agreed under the amended Brownfield policy (Aug 2026)
Strategic role: The inland anchor of Pakistan&apos;s fuel system — refinery, 2,000+ km pipeline network and strategic storage under one company
Risks: Import dependence via one coastal pipeline corridor; currency and payment pressures; policy-implementation delays</description>
