				<Placemark>
					<name>Cnergyico Oil Refining Complex, Mouza Kund</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Owner: Cnergyico Pk Limited (formerly Byco) — Pakistan&apos;s largest refiner, ~36% of national capacity
Capacity: 156,000 b/d nameplate across two hydroskimming units — ORC-I (36,000, from 2004) and ORC-II (120,000, from 2012–15) — at Mouza Kund, Hub, Balochistan, ~50 km from Karachi
Feedstock: Imported crude landed at Pakistan&apos;s only Single Point Mooring — a VLCC-capable buoy ~11.5 km offshore in 26 m of water, linked to a 130,000 t tank farm
Main products: Gasoline, high-speed diesel, jet fuel, kerosene, naphtha, LPG, furnace oil — the simple configuration yields heavy furnace-oil volumes
Markets: Domestic OMCs; since July 2025 ~95% of fuel-oil output is exported, driven by domestic taxation
Recent: Production halted temporarily in May 2025 on product oversupply (&quot;ullage&quot;); a $1.2bn three-phase upgrade planned — Euro-V fuels, then Pakistan&apos;s largest FCC, then capacity toward 200,000 b/d
Strategic role: The import valve of Pakistan&apos;s fuel system — the SPM is the country&apos;s only deep-water crude gateway
Risks: Low complexity and furnace-oil dependence; chronic under-utilisation; refining-margin swings; financing the upgrade</description>
