				<Placemark>
					<name>National Refinery Limited, Korangi</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Owner: Attock Group — Attock Refinery 25%, Pakistan Oilfields 25%, Islamic Development Bank 15%
Capacity: ~64,000–70,000 b/d nominal across fuel and lube segments; operating since 1963, next to PRL on Korangi Creek, Karachi
Feedstock: ~70% imported light crude, ~30% heavy — the heavy share is deliberate: it feeds Pakistan&apos;s only lube base-oil production
Main products: Fuels (Euro-V diesel already achieved), lubricant base oils, asphalt, BTX aromatics, waxes — the country&apos;s sole lube refiner
Markets: Domestic fuels; lube base oils and specialities domestically and for export
Recent: A $300–800m hybrid clean-fuels and bottom-of-barrel project under study (Wood feasibility) — furnace-oil output to fall from ~2,250 t/day to ~250; capacity rise to 70,000 b/d considered
Strategic role: The specialist of the five — Pakistan&apos;s lubricants supply depends on this single site
Risks: Heavy losses in FY2025; furnace-oil exposure until the upgrade; single-site lube dependence for the whole country</description>
