				<Placemark>
					<name>Eni Gela Biorefinery</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Renewables: Dedicated biorefinery — the entire site converted from crude to HVO
Owner: Eni
Capacity: ~750,000 t/yr of hydrotreated renewable diesel and bio-jet via Eni&apos;s Ecofining process — one of Europe&apos;s flagship refinery conversions, running since 2019 on used cooking oils and waste fats
Feedstock: Waste and residue lipids, increasingly agri-feedstocks from Eni&apos;s African supply projects
Main products: HVO renewable diesel, bio-naphtha, bio-LPG, SAF streams
Markets: Italian and European renewable-fuel mandates
Recent: The former 105,000 b/d crude refinery closed in 2014 after years of losses — the conversion turned Sicily&apos;s south coast into a transition showcase rather than an industrial ruin
Strategic role: The counter-story of the Sicilian hub — one coast prices fossil cargoes while the other manufactures their replacement; joins the map&apos;s renewables-filter family
Risks: Feedstock competition and cost; mandate-policy dependence; small scale against fossil economics</description>
