				<Placemark>
					<name>Westridge Marine Terminal</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Owner/Operator: Trans Mountain Corporation (Canadian federal Crown corporation)
Role: Pacific crude export gateway — marine terminus of the Trans Mountain system; export capacity up to ~630,000 b/d within the expanded ~890,000 b/d system (May 2024); also handles aviation fuel for Vancouver airport
Berths / vessel size: Three Aframax berths (was one before the expansion); Second Narrows draft limits loads to ~75–80% of a 550,000–725,000 bbl cargo; up to ~34 tankers + 3 barges/month at full utilisation
Main markets: Asia-Pacific (notably China), California, western Canada
Recent: The Trans Mountain Expansion nearly tripled system capacity from 300,000 b/d
Risks: Draft and tidal limits through Vancouver Harbour&apos;s Second Narrows; harbour transit constraints</description>
