					<name>Trans Mountain Burnaby Crude Oil Storage &amp; Distribution Terminal</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Owner/Operator: Trans Mountain Corporation
Role: Final inland terminal of the Trans Mountain system — receipt, storage, segregation, blending and redistribution of western Canadian crude (incl. diluted bitumen) and selected products; no tanker loading — export crude moves on to Westridge by the underground connection
Storage capacity: ~5.5 million barrels in 26 tanks
Connectivity: Westridge Marine Terminal, the Parkland Burnaby refinery, regional BC terminals and, via the system, Washington State refineries; system capacity ~890,000 b/d since May 2024 (was 300,000)
Risks: Dense urban interface on Burnaby Mountain (full fire-protection and emergency-response infrastructure); single-system dependence for Pacific exports</description>
