					<name>Sheskharis Oil Terminal</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Owner/Operator: Transneft system (Chernomortransneft)
Role: Russia&apos;s main Black Sea crude and products export terminal at Novorossiysk — the southern outlet of the Transneft network
Capacity: ~700,000 b/d of crude loadings in normal recent conditions; volumes vary with schedules and disruptions
Berths / vessel size: Multiple berths; the largest deep-water berth takes tankers to ~250,000 dwt / ~19 m draft (Suezmax, some VLCC-scale operations)
Storage capacity: Integrated with the inland Grushevaya Balka tank farm — combined &gt;1 million m³
Main markets: Mediterranean, Türkiye and Asia via the Black Sea and Turkish Straits
Risks: Disruptions here move a significant share of Russian seaborne exports — and international prices; Turkish Straits passage</description>
