Role: Export and storage terminal for Iraqi crude arriving via the Iraq–Türkiye pipeline (parallel 40-inch and 46-inch lines, ~70.9 Mt/yr ≈ 1.4–1.5 million b/d nominal)
Berths / vessel size: 1,950 m marine jetty loading up to four tankers simultaneously
Storage capacity: ~11 million barrels (April 2026); expansion planned to 45 million
Connectivity: Iraq–Türkiye pipeline, Ceyhan–Kırıkkale line, the wider Ceyhan energy hub
Recent: Iraqi exports resumed after a prolonged interruption, but flows remain well below nominal capacity
Risks: Dependence on Iraq–Türkiye pipeline politics; utilisation far under capacity</description>
