				<Placemark>
					<name>Skikda Oil Terminal</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Owner/Operator: Sonatrach and affiliated refinery, LNG, pipeline and petrochemical divisions
Role: Integrated storage complex between the RA1K refinery, the LNG plant and the hydrocarbon port — receipt, segregation, buffer storage, blending, refinery feed management and export-cargo preparation
Handles: Crude, condensate, gasoline, diesel, jet, naphtha, fuel oil, LPG, LNG feedstocks, aromatics
Storage capacity: No consolidated public figure for the oil tank farms; the LNG complex alone holds 246,000 m³ in three tanks
Connectivity: RA1K and RA2K refineries, GL1K LNG complex, petrochemical plants, inland pipelines, marine berths
Risks: Tank fires, vapour release, spills, overfilling and cascading incidents in a dense industrial zone</description>
