					<description>Status: Operational
Owner/Operator: Shell SPDC — Renaissance Africa Energy since March 2025 — on behalf of the NNPC joint venture
Role: Onshore reception and storage for Bonny Light — crude from the Trans Niger Pipeline and the Nembe Creek Trunk Line is received, commingled and held before export; no harbour or quay — crude leaves by submarine pipeline to the offshore loading buoys
Capacity: ~250,000 b/d rated throughput
Storage capacity: ~5.7 million barrels (NUPRC crude-terminal register)
Risks: Dependence on the two feeder trunklines; Niger Delta operating environment</description>
