				<Placemark id="DD4F791C5111D38B2695">
					<name>Kulevi Oil Terminal</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Owner/Operator: SOCAR (SOCAR Georgia Petroleum)
Role: Georgia&apos;s principal Black Sea oil gateway — crude and products arrive mainly by rail from Azerbaijan (and, per EU and OCCRP reporting, Russia), are stored and loaded onto tankers
Storage capacity: One of Georgia&apos;s largest multi-tank farms
Connectivity: Rail link to Baku; marine berths; since 2024–25 also handles cargo for the adjacent, separately owned Kulevi refinery
Recent: Kept transshipping Russian-linked cargoes through 2025–26 under Western scrutiny; the terminal itself was not named in the EU&apos;s 21st sanctions package (July 2026), unlike the refinery; a 2024 Black Sea spill was linked to operations in the area
Risks: Sanctions scrutiny; spill history; rail-logistics dependence</description>
