				<Placemark>
					<name>Vadinar Terminal (Nayara Energy)</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Owner/Operator: Nayara Energy (Rosneft ~49.13%, Kesani Enterprises ~49.13%)
Role: Captive deep-water port of the 400,000 b/d Vadinar refinery — the main entry gate for discounted Russian Urals into India since 2022, and a major gasoline/diesel export hub toward Africa, the Middle East and Asia
Berths / vessel size: VLCC-capable SPM buoys (to ~350,000 dwt); products on MR/LR tankers at jetty berths
Storage capacity: One of India&apos;s largest tank farms
Connectivity: ~30 km from Reliance Jamnagar — the Gulf of Kutch is the world&apos;s densest refining zone (~1.8 million b/d combined)
Recent: July 2026 — first confirmed Indian fuel shipment TO Russia: 356,000 bbl of gasoline loaded at Vadinar, transshipped STS off Port Said, delivered at Vitino (White Sea) — a rare reversal of the usual flow
Risks: EU sanctions on Nayara via the Rosneft stake — shadow-fleet logistics, payment and insurance frictions; Arabian Sea cyclones</description>
