				<Placemark>
					<name>Vitino Terminal</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Owner/Operator: Rusneftekhim (bought with the Belomorsk terminal in 2009, ~$50m); restarted in the sanctions era
Role: Small White Sea rail-to-tanker terminal — the region&apos;s only oil transshipment port, revived as a discreet Arctic outlet far from the closely watched Baltic routes
Berths / vessel size: One deep-water berth plus two smaller — three tankers simultaneously; ships to 230 m length, 10.9 m draft, ~80,000 t cargo (mid-size only)
Recent: Modernisation targets ≥4 Mt/yr of products (diesel, naphtha) — its pre-2014 peak, when it shipped for Lukoil, Gazprom Neft and Novatek before flows moved to the Baltic and the port went bankrupt. July 2026: destination of the first confirmed Indian gasoline delivery to Russia (356,000 bbl ex-Vadinar)
Risks: Sanctions-era opacity; Arctic ice and navigation; rail dependence</description>
