				<Placemark>
					<name>Ras Tanura–Juaymah</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Owner/Operator: Saudi Aramco
Role: Saudi Arabia&apos;s principal crude export complex — the North Pier, Sea Island terminals and Juaymah single-point moorings load Arabian Light, Extra Light and Medium plus LPG and products; integrated with the ~550,000 b/d Ras Tanura refinery
Berths / vessel size: Fixed offshore terminals and SPMs designed for deep-draft crude tankers (VLCC)
Connectivity: Aramco&apos;s trunk-pipeline and storage network from the Eastern Province fields
Main markets: Primarily Asia — China, India, Japan
Recent: Crude loadings resumed in June 2026 after a prolonged disruption; the refinery was shut as a precaution after a 2 March 2026 drone strike
Risks: Hormuz dependence; drone and missile exposure; regional conflict</description>
