				<Placemark>
					<name>LOOP–Clovelly–St. James Crude Hub</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Owner/Operator: LOOP LLC (offshore terminal, subsea pipelines, Clovelly Hub); private operators around St. James
Role: Deep-water crude import/export, storage, blending and inland-distribution hub — the offshore terminal ~18 nm off Louisiana can both unload and load deep-draft tankers
Crude flows: Imported medium and heavy crude, Gulf of Mexico production, domestic light crude and export cargoes, moving between the terminal, Clovelly storage and the St. James trading centre
Connectivity: LOCAP and Capline onward to Lower Mississippi and Midwest refineries
Main markets: Louisiana refineries; the Midwest via Capline
Risks: Hurricane exposure; concentration of deep-draft flows on one hub</description>
					<LookAt>
						<longitude>-90.22457012593216</longitude>
						<latitude>30.23964645435963</latitude>
						<altitude>0</altitude>
