				<Placemark>
					<name>Valdez Marine Terminal</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Owner/Operator: Alyeska Pipeline Service Company
Role: Sole maritime outlet for Alaska North Slope crude — terminus of the 800-mile Trans-Alaska Pipeline System (TAPS)
Berths / vessel size: Two operational loading berths; vapour management, ballast-water treatment and dedicated spill-response infrastructure
Storage capacity: 13 tanks in service, ~6.6 million barrels of working inventory
Main markets: US West Coast refineries — Washington State and California
Risks: Single-outlet dependence on TAPS; Prince William Sound marine risk (extensive dedicated spill-response fleet)</description>
					<LookAt>
						<longitude>-146.3431798517328</longitude>
						<latitude>61.10344680654605</latitude>
