				<Placemark id="0B2BEEDECD3F32C45703">
					<name>Houston Ship Channel / Buffalo Bayou Industrial Corridor</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Owner/Operator: Port Houston maintains the public channel; refineries, terminals and docks privately operated
Role: One of the world&apos;s largest concentrations of refining, petrochemical, storage and marine-terminal infrastructure — Buffalo Bayou, widened and deepened into the upper Houston Ship Channel, brings ocean ships deep into the metro area
Main facilities: Refineries, petrochemical plants, product and chemical terminals, LPG/NGL handling, tank farms, ship and barge docks, pipeline interconnections, rail
Connectivity: Linked to Texas crude systems and Gulf export routes; distinct from the Mont Belvieu NGL hub further north-east
Strategic role: The heart of the US refining-petrochemical complex and its export logistics — one of the most strategically important industrial waterways in the country
Risks: Hurricanes; channel congestion and closures; industrial incidents; fog</description>
