				<Placemark id="ADDEPRT000000000001">
					<name>Port of Eilat</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Owner/Operator: Privatised 2013, operated under concession (Papo Maritime); the EAPC oil jetty sits within the port area
Role: Israel&apos;s only Red Sea commercial port — vehicle imports from Asia, potash and mineral exports; the one Israeli gateway avoiding both the Mediterranean and Suez
Recent: The Houthi campaign against Red Sea shipping from late 2023 collapsed traffic (revenues down ~85–90%), pushing the port into insolvency proceedings in 2024; activity remains far below pre-war levels
Strategic role: A live case study of chokepoint economics — the port&apos;s paralysis is the direct cost of Bab el-Mandeb insecurity, visible on one map with the strait itself
Risks: Chokepoint dependence; financial fragility; competition from Jordan&apos;s Aqaba next door</description>
					<styleUrl>#msn_ylw-pushpin0</styleUrl>
					<Point>
						<coordinates>34.9579861768777,29.5404905887817,0</coordinates>
