				<Placemark>
					<name>Port of Rotterdam – Energy, Refining &amp; Logistics Hub</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Owner/Operator: Port of Rotterdam Authority; terminals, refineries and plants privately operated
Role: Europe&apos;s largest port and the ARA market&apos;s central physical hub — crude, products, LNG, biofuels, chemicals and containers; historically ~95–100 Mt/yr of crude enters here for Dutch, Belgian and German refineries
Main facilities: Crude and product terminals, independent tank farms, LNG import, the Pernis / ExxonMobil / BP / Gunvor refining cluster, petrochemicals, bunkering
Connectivity: Rhine–Meuse waterway system, rail and road, and pipelines toward Antwerp, Amsterdam and Germany (RRP)
Strategic role: Northwest Europe&apos;s main entry, processing, blending and redistribution point for energy — the price-forming end of the Rhine story on this map
Risks: Refinery outages; Rhine water-level constraints; North Sea weather; congestion; labour; carbon regulation</description>
