				<Placemark>
					<name>Port of Antwerp-Bruges – Refining &amp; Petrochemical Hub</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Owner/Operator: Port of Antwerp-Bruges Authority; industrial facilities privately operated
Role: Major integrated refining, petrochemical and liquid-bulk hub — anchored by the TotalEnergies and ExxonMobil refineries and Europe&apos;s largest integrated chemical cluster, exchanging feedstocks, hydrogen and steam by pipeline
Main facilities: Refineries, steam crackers, chemical plants, a large independent tank-storage sector, LNG at Zeebrugge
Connectivity: Pipeline, barge, rail and road to Rotterdam and the Rhine-Ruhr hinterland
Strategic role: One of the world&apos;s most integrated refining-chemical locations, with global maritime access and deep European hinterland reach
Risks: Cracker and refinery outages; strikes; Scheldt navigation restrictions; high European energy costs; tightening environmental regulation</description>
