				<Placemark>
					<name>Port of Amsterdam – Petroleum Products &amp; Storage Hub</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Owner/Operator: Port of Amsterdam Authority; storage terminals privately operated
Role: The gasoline capital of the ARA system — storage, blending, transshipment and trading of refined products rather than crude refining; bunker supply for sea and river vessels
Main facilities: Independent product terminals, blending installations, barge loading, distribution warehouses
Connectivity: North Sea access via IJmuiden; inland waterways toward Rotterdam, Antwerp and the Rhine
Recent: Coal handling to be phased out by 2030
Strategic role: The flexible storage-and-blending leg of the ARA benchmark market — gasoline, diesel, fuel oil and biofuels
Risks: Product contamination and tank fires; North Sea Canal access; declining fossil demand; gasoline-trade volatility</description>
