				<Placemark>
					<name>Singapore–Jurong Island</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Owner/Operator: Singapore agencies (MPA, JTC, EDB) coordinate; facilities operated by international energy, chemical and terminal companies
Role: Global oil-trading, refining, petrochemical, storage and bunkering hub — the world&apos;s leading marine-fuel bunkering centre and Asia&apos;s principal price-discovery point
Main facilities: The ExxonMobil and SRC refineries plus Aster&apos;s Bukom platform, petrochemical complexes, independent tank terminals, underground caverns, LNG infrastructure, STS bunkering
Connectivity: Astride the Malacca/Singapore Straits between Middle Eastern supply and Asian demand; regional base for Vitol, Trafigura, Glencore, Shell, BP and PetroChina trading desks
Strategic role: Asia&apos;s physical oil-trading centre — refining, storage and bunkering in one strait-side location
Risks: Malacca congestion; imported-feedstock dependence; terminal and refinery outages; petrochemical overcapacity; Middle East supply disruption</description>
					<LookAt>
						<longitude>103.6993701</longitude>
						<latitude>1.2851399</latitude>
