					<name>Ningbo–Zhoushan Port – Crude Import, Refining &amp; Bunkering Hub</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Owner/Operator: Ningbo Zhoushan Port Group; terminals, refineries and storage run by state and private companies
Role: One of the world&apos;s largest ports by tonnage and one of China&apos;s main seaborne crude gateways — deep-water crude terminals, storage farms, LNG, and supply to the Zhenhai complex and the Zhoushan greenfield refining zone; Zhoushan is also China&apos;s leading bunkering centre
Connectivity: Middle Eastern, Russian, Atlantic Basin and West African cargoes into the Yangtze Delta refining system
Strategic role: The intake valve of eastern China&apos;s refining industry and marine-fuel supply
Risks: Typhoons; congestion; refinery outages; petrochemical overcapacity; East China Sea shipping disruption; imported-crude dependence</description>
