					<description>Status: Operational
Owner/Operator: Ulsan Port Authority; industry operated by SK Energy, S-OIL and others
Role: One of Asia&apos;s most concentrated refining areas — deep-water oil berths, refinery jetties, chemical terminals and tank farms serving the SK Energy Ulsan complex and S-OIL Onsan nearby
Connectivity: Marine access to Asian shipping lanes; integrated with base oils, aromatics and polymer production; shipyards alongside
Recent: Growing focus on hydrogen, CCUS and cleaner marine fuels
Strategic role: A pillar of Korean energy security and a major products and petrochemicals export outlet to NE/SE Asia
Risks: Imported-crude and Hormuz dependence; typhoons; refinery outages; petrochemical margin weakness; industrial accidents</description>
