					<description>Status: Operational
Owner/Operator: Yeosu Gwangyang Port Authority; industry operated by GS Caltex, petrochemical and steel companies
Role: Refining, petrochemical and bulk-industrial hub on Korea&apos;s southern coast — anchored by the GS Caltex Yeosu refinery, with crude and product berths, petrochemical jetties, tank farms and steel logistics
Connectivity: Crude in from the Middle East and beyond; fuels, naphtha, aromatics and derivatives out to Asian markets; LNG and power alongside
Recent: Korea is reviewing a restructuring of the Yeosu petrochemical complex amid weak margins
Strategic role: One of Korea&apos;s core energy-industrial port systems — fuel production, chemicals and heavy industry in one coastal hub
Risks: Imported-crude dependence; typhoons; refinery outages; petrochemical oversupply; regional trade disruption</description>
