					<description>Status: Operational
Owner/Operator: Reliance Industries (industrial assets); Sikka and nearby marine facilities
Role: The port system of the world&apos;s largest refining site — very large crude-import terminals, refinery jetties and product-export berths serving Reliance&apos;s ~1.4 million b/d Jamnagar complex
Connectivity: A highly diversified global crude slate in; one of the world&apos;s largest refined-product export flows out, especially middle distillates
Strategic role: With Vadinar ~30 km away, makes the Gulf of Kutch the world&apos;s densest refining zone (~1.8 million b/d combined)
Risks: Imported-crude dependence; Gulf shipping disruption; cyclones; maintenance outages; refining-margin volatility</description>
