					<description>Status: Operational
Owner/Operator: Multiple operators, including Transneft system assets; commercial and industrial facilities alongside
Role: One of Russia&apos;s principal Black Sea export gateways — crude, diesel, fuel oil, naphtha, plus grain, metals and containers; includes the Sheskharis terminal and sits beside the CPC loading systems for Kazakh crude
Connectivity: Linked to Russia&apos;s domestic pipeline network and inland storage; exports transit the Turkish Straits to the Mediterranean and Asia
Recent: Repeated attacks and temporary loading interruptions have affected export reliability during the war
Strategic role: A critical outlet for Russian and Kazakh seaborne exports — disruptions here move global prices
Risks: Drone and missile attacks; Black Sea security; Turkish Straits congestion; sanctions; terminal damage; pipeline-supply interruptions</description>
