					<description>Status: Operational
Owner/Operator: DP World UAE; the adjacent Jebel Ali Free Zone hosts thousands of companies
Role: The Middle East&apos;s largest container and industrial logistics hub — four container terminals, 100+ berths, ~25 km of quay, ~19.4 million TEU capacity; includes ENOC&apos;s Jebel Ali refinery (expanded ~140,000 → 210,000 b/d), lubricant and blending plants
Connectivity: The main distribution gateway between global shipping routes, Dubai and the Gulf economy
Strategic role: Primarily a container/logistics giant with a meaningful refining and fuel-blending side — the commercial counterpart to Fujairah&apos;s oil-storage role
Risks: Hormuz disruption; congestion; cyberattacks; regional military tension; competition from Khalifa, Hamad and Saudi hubs</description>
