					<name>Yanbu Industrial Port</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Owner/Operator: King Fahd Industrial Port under the Saudi Ports Authority; Aramco operates the principal crude and product terminals
Role: Saudi Arabia&apos;s principal Red Sea export outlet — Arabian Light and Super Light crude plus products, LPG, naphtha and petrochemicals; VLCC berths up to ~500,000 dwt
Main facilities: Yanbu North and South crude terminals, tank farms, product jetties, and the YASREF (~400,000 b/d), SAMREF (~400,000 b/d) and Aramco Yanbu refineries
Connectivity: Fed from eastern Saudi Arabia by the East–West Pipeline (Petroline)
Recent: The pivot point of the 2026 Hormuz closure — Saudi loadings shifted here, with barrels routing onward into SUMED after the July Houthi threat
Strategic role: The reason Saudi crude can reach Europe and the Atlantic without Hormuz
Risks: East–West Pipeline disruption; Bab el-Mandeb and Red Sea security; refinery outages; concentration of large facilities in one cluster</description>
