					<name>Ras Laffan Port</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Owner/Operator: QatarEnergy owns and operates the port; QatarEnergy LNG and partners run the processing complexes
Role: The world&apos;s largest LNG-export facility — liquefaction trains, Q-Flex/Q-Max berths, plus condensate refining (Laffan 1 &amp; 2, ~306,000 b/d combined), Pearl and Oryx GTL, helium and sulphur
Handles: LNG, condensate, LPG, naphtha, jet, GTL products, ethane, sulphur
Connectivity: Offshore-to-onshore pipelines from the North Field; export lanes via Hormuz
Strategic role: The central export gateway of Qatar&apos;s North Field — a gas hub whose condensate and naphtha streams matter to oil markets too
Risks: Hormuz disruption; LNG-train outages; concentrated infrastructure; specialised-equipment dependence; military escalation</description>
