					<description>Status: Operational
Owner/Operator: Tanger Med Port Authority; terminals under concession (APM Terminals, Eurogate, Marsa Maroc)
Role: Africa&apos;s leading container-transshipment hub on the Strait of Gibraltar — 11.1+ million TEU in 2025 — with a hydrocarbon terminal for product imports, storage, blending and bunkering; no major refinery
Connectivity: At the Europe–Africa–Atlantic–Mediterranean crossroads, ~40 km east of Tangier; rail and industrial zones inland
Strategic role: A maritime bridge between Europe and Africa whose fuel side serves Moroccan demand and strait-side bunkering
Risks: Gibraltar congestion; strong winds; container-network disruption; cyberattacks; dependence on transshipment activity</description>
