					<description>Status: Operational
Owner/Operator: Lekki Port LFTZ Enterprise under Nigerian port supervision; Dangote Industries separately owns the adjacent refinery and its marine facilities
Role: Deep-sea port + Africa&apos;s largest refinery in one zone — a 1,200 m container quay (~2.7 million TEU design), dry-bulk and liquid berths, and the Dangote marine-loading system
Connectivity: Gulf of Guinea access east of the congested Apapa/Tin Can complexes; tank farms and the refinery&apos;s dedicated jetties
Strategic role: Nigeria&apos;s emerging downstream hub — domestic fuel supply plus regional product exports from the 650,000 b/d refinery
