					<name>Port of Durban</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Owner/Operator: Transnet National Ports Authority (landlord); Transnet Port Terminals runs the main terminals; private liquid-bulk operators
Role: Sub-Saharan Africa&apos;s principal container gateway and South Africa&apos;s main fuel-import point — containers, vehicles, and the Island View liquid-bulk precinct for gasoline, diesel, jet and chemicals
Recent: The ~180,000 b/d SAPREF refinery — historically the country&apos;s largest — has ceased refining, deepening import dependence
Connectivity: Pipeline and rail toward the inland demand centres around Johannesburg
Strategic role: The coastal entry point for the fuels that feed South Africa&apos;s largest inland market
Risks: Container congestion; road/rail bottlenecks; flooding; power failures; labour disruption; fuel-import dependence; prolonged outages at former refining sites</description>
