					<description>Status: Operational
Owner/Operator: Transnet National Ports Authority; Transnet Port Terminals (iron ore), Strategic Fuel Fund (crude storage), Sunrise Energy (LPG)
Role: South Africa&apos;s strategic crude-storage location and dominant deep-water iron-ore export gateway — a crude jetty for very large tankers, pipelines to strategic storage, and an LPG import terminal; no refinery
Connectivity: ~110 km north of Cape Town, close to the Cape of Good Hope shipping routes
Strategic role: National crude reserves plus a position on the Cape route — relevant whenever chokepoint closures push tankers around Africa
Risks: Atlantic weather; iron-ore railway disruption; storage-system failures; limited local refining demand; dependence on a few specialised terminals</description>
