					<description>Status: Operational
Owner/Operator: Djibouti Ports and Free Zones Authority; container, multipurpose and petroleum facilities run by state-controlled and commercial entities incl. the Horizon oil terminal (~371,000 m³)
Role: Red Sea transit, fuel-import and Horn of Africa logistics hub next to Bab el-Mandeb — containers, diesel, gasoline, jet, LPG, grain; the Damerjog liquid-bulk zone under development
Connectivity: The maritime gateway for landlocked Ethiopia (rail-connected); bunkering and naval presence at the strait
Strategic role: The listening post of Bab el-Mandeb — fuel supply and logistics at the exact point where the 2023–26 shipping crisis plays out
Risks: Red Sea military activity; attacks on shipping; Ethiopian-transit dependence; regional instability; port competition</description>
