					<name>Port of Corpus Christi</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Owner/Operator: Port of Corpus Christi Authority (channel and public infrastructure); private midstream and refining operators
Role: The leading US crude-export gateway — WTI Midland and Eagle Ford barrels; exports generally exceeded 2 million b/d through 2025 and early 2026, ~93–97% of outbound crude movements
Main facilities: Large crude-export terminals at Ingleside and Corpus Christi, refinery docks, independent tank farms, deep-water berths
Connectivity: Long-distance pipelines from the Permian Basin and Eagle Ford
Strategic role: The principal maritime outlet for Permian grades — self-described largest US energy-export gateway
Risks: Hurricanes and fog; channel closures; pipeline outages; terminal concentration; congestion at export peaks</description>
