					<name>Port Arthur–Beaumont / Sabine–Neches Waterway</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Owner/Operator: Ports of Port Arthur and Beaumont (public marine infrastructure); private refinery docks, terminals and pipelines
Role: A crude intake and refining hub rather than an export hub — home to the Motiva Port Arthur, ExxonMobil Beaumont, Valero and TotalEnergies systems, including two of the largest US refineries
Connectivity: Texas and Louisiana crude pipelines, regional storage hubs, the Gulf Intracoastal Waterway, rail
Strategic role: One of the most important US destinations for domestic and imported refinery feedstock — processed locally rather than re-exported
Risks: Hurricanes and flooding; refinery fires and hazardous releases; channel congestion; dependence on a highly concentrated refining complex</description>
