					<description>Status: Operational
Owner/Operator: Port Freeport (channel and public facilities); private crude terminals and pipelines
Role: Crude, condensate and NGL export and pipeline port ~60 miles south of Houston; the nearby Sweeny refining-petrochemical system creates regional feedstock demand
Connectivity: The Seaway system links Freeport&apos;s marine docks with Cushing and Houston-area markets; Texas crude pipelines; Gulf Intracoastal Waterway
Strategic role: A secondary but significant Texas crude-export port — self-identified as a leading US exporter of crude and NGLs
Risks: Hurricanes; channel closures; pipeline disruption; competition from Corpus Christi and Houston; dependence on private terminal availability</description>
