				<Placemark>
					<name>Port of Texas City</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Owner/Operator: Texas City Terminal Railway Company; refinery and crude terminals privately operated
Role: Crude import, refinery-supply and storage port on Galveston Bay — centred on Marathon&apos;s ~631,000 b/cd Galveston Bay refinery and Valero Texas City
Connectivity: Seaway infrastructure links the port to Cushing and Houston-area systems; rail via the Terminal Railway; Aframax and Suezmax tanker access
Recent: A separate low-carbon fuel-trading hub is being developed
Strategic role: A major crude-receiving and refinery-feed port at the entrance of the Houston Ship Channel system
Risks: Hurricanes and storm surge; refinery accidents; ship-channel disruption; ageing infrastructure; concentration on a few large refineries</description>
