					</Point>
				</Placemark>
				<Placemark>
					<name>Port of Skikda</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Owner/Operator: Entreprise Portuaire de Skikda; hydrocarbon assets integrated with Sonatrach operations
Role: One of Algeria&apos;s three principal petroleum ports — crude, condensate, products, LPG, LNG and aromatics; ~30 Mt/yr of hydrocarbon transit
Berths / vessel size: Dedicated crude berth to ~100,000 dwt plus two offshore SPMs serving VLCC-scale tankers (~320,000 t); LNG and product jetties
Connectivity: Fed by the OK1 crude and NK1 condensate pipelines from Haoud El Hamra; serves the RA1K/RA2K refineries and GL1K LNG complex
Strategic role: The main maritime outlet of the Skikda refining-LNG-petrochemical zone — Mediterranean delivery two days from European ports
Risks: Tanker accidents and spills; LNG incidents; industrial fires; berth outages; Mediterranean weather; inland pipeline disruption</description>
					<LookAt>
						<longitude>6.973724551104133</longitude>
						<latitude>36.87068648093334</latitude>
