				</Placemark>
				<Placemark>
					<name>Brofjorden port</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Hub: Brofjorden port — VAROPreem Lysekil crude &amp; product terminal
Classification: Sweden&apos;s largest oil port; the deep-water gateway of the Lysekil refinery
Location: Brofjorden fjord, near Lysekil, west coast of Sweden (~130 km north of Gothenburg)
Owner/Operator: VAROPreem — the port is owned by the refinery itself
Infrastructure: One crude berth (28 m depth, tankers up to 500,000 dwt) and five product jetties; ~800,000 m³ of crude stored in rock caverns; ~22 Mt of cargo a year
Berths / vessel size: Full VLCC access — largest ever call ~470,000 dwt
Handles: Crude imports (mostly sour/medium grades) and product exports — two-thirds of Lysekil&apos;s output goes to NW Europe by sea
Connectivity: Pipeline to the refinery; no rail, poor roads — everything moves by ship
Strategic role: Unrestricted VLCC access gives Lysekil some of the cheapest crude freight in Europe — a core competitive edge
Risks: Single-port dependence for the whole refinery; Skagerrak weather</description>
