				<Placemark>
					<name>Port of Gothenburg</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Terminal: Port of Gothenburg — Energy Port (Skarvik, Rya, Torshamnen)
Classification: The Nordics&apos; largest energy port; Sweden&apos;s main import/export gateway for products
Location: Hisingen, Gothenburg — product harbours at Skarvik/Rya, crude harbour at Torshamnen (~6 km west)
Owner/Operator: Port of Gothenburg; independent tank operators plus the two on-site refiners, VAROPreem and St1
Infrastructure: Product and chemical jetties, Torshamnen crude berth (~19 m draft, pipeline-linked to both refineries), tank-farm clusters at Skarvik, Rya and Viken
Handles: Crude in; gasoline, diesel, jet, HVO, fuel oil, chemicals and bunkers out — about half of Sweden&apos;s petroleum products pass through here
Connectivity: Pipelines to the Preem and St1 refineries; export point for VAROPreem&apos;s Redefine HVO100
Strategic role: The products-side pole of Swedish refining, paired with Brofjorden on the crude side
Risks: Urban-port constraints; concentration of national product imports at one hub</description>
