						</coordinates>
					</LineString>
				</Placemark>
				<Placemark>
					<name>Keystone Cushing Extension (Steele City–Cushing)</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Route: Steele City, Nebraska (junction of the Keystone mainline from Hardisty, Alberta) → Kansas → Cushing
Owner/Operator: TC Energy
Capacity: Part of the ~600,000+ b/d Keystone system&apos;s southern flows
Handles: Canadian heavy and synthetic crude into the hub&apos;s tanks — the northern feed of the WTI delivery point
Recent: The December 2022 Mill Creek rupture in Kansas — the largest US onshore spill in a decade — happened on this segment, cutting deliveries and briefly moving the WTI market
Strategic role: The pipe that makes Cushing a continental hub rather than a Texan one — Alberta barrels priced against Oklahoma paper
Risks: Spill history and regulatory pressure; upstream dependence on one mainline; heavy-light quality management in shared tanks</description>
					<styleUrl>#op30</styleUrl>
