						</coordinates>
					</LineString>
				</Placemark>
				<Placemark>
					<name>Basin Pipeline (Permian–Wichita Falls–Cushing)</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Route: Jal/Wink area in the Permian Basin → Midland → Wichita Falls → Cushing
Owner/Operator: Plains All American
Capacity: ~500,000+ b/d
Handles: West Texas Intermediate in the literal sense — Permian barrels moving to the delivery point that named them
Recent: The shale era inverted its importance: most Permian growth now flows straight to Corpus Christi and Houston, making Basin the optional route and the Cushing–Midland spread the signal of which path pays
Strategic role: The historic artery between the basin and the benchmark — WTI&apos;s own supply line
Risks: Structural competition from Permian-to-Gulf pipelines; utilisation swings; ageing infrastructure</description>
					<styleUrl>#op30</styleUrl>
