							56.03,22.19,0 56.48,22.35,0 57.52000000000001,22.38,0 57.77,22.93,0 58.02,23.31,0 58.5,23.63,0 
						</coordinates>
					</LineString>
				</Placemark>
				<Placemark>
					<name>Ras Markaz – Duqm Refinery Crude Pipeline</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Route: Ras Markaz Crude Oil Park → ~80 km north along the coastal corridor → the OQ8 Duqm refinery&apos;s dedicated crude tanks (eight tanks at the refinery end); operational since April 2023
Owner/Operator: OTTCO / OQ8 system
Handles: The refinery&apos;s full crude diet — Kuwaiti and Omani grades landed at the SPM and stored at Ras Markaz, delivered on refinery demand
Strategic role: The line that makes Duqm work — an outside-the-strait refinery fed from an outside-the-strait terminal, the only link in its supply chain that touches no chokepoint at all
Risks: Single feed line for a 230,000 b/d plant; remote-corridor maintenance; upstream dependence on the tanker shuttle until the national grid connection exists</description>
					<styleUrl>#op30</styleUrl>
