				<Placemark id="ADDMVL00000000000001">
					<name>Rostock–Schwedt Pipeline (MVL)</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Route: Rostock oil port (Baltic Sea) → PCK Schwedt refinery, ~200 km
Owner/Operator: PCK Raffinerie GmbH
Capacity: Limited — historically able to load the refinery at roughly half its nameplate; a ~€400m upgrade has been pursued to raise throughput
Recent: Became Schwedt&apos;s lifeline after Germany ended Russian pipeline crude imports in January 2023
Strategic role: The substitute artery for the Druzhba supply that fed Schwedt for five decades — seaborne barrels landed at Rostock reach the Berlin fuel market through this line
Risks: Capacity bottleneck versus refinery nameplate; dependence on Baltic tanker deliveries and port logistics</description>
