				<Placemark>
					<name>Druzhba - 1 Hungary connection</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Route: Šahy (southern Slovakia, on the Ipeľ) → Hungarian border at Drégelypalánk → Százhalombatta (MOL Danube refinery)
Owner/Operator: Transpetrol / MOL
Handles: Crude in either direction between the two southern Druzhba lines — Slovak and Hungarian supply can back each other up
Strategic role: The reason the two lines behave as one system — crude reaching Hungary via Adria/JANAF can flow up to Slovakia through Százhalombatta and Šahy, the route that supplied Slovnaft during the 2026 outage; MOL&apos;s plan to run Százhalombatta, Bratislava and Pančevo as one network rests on links like this
Risks: Limited capacity relative to full refinery demand; both ends depend on the same Adria fallback</description>
					<styleUrl>#op30</styleUrl>
