				<Placemark id="ADDFPS00000000000001">
					<name>Forties Pipeline System (FPS)</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Route: Forties Unity platform (central North Sea) → Cruden Bay landfall (169 km offshore) → Kinneil, Grangemouth (209 km onshore) → Dalmeny tank farm → Hound Point export jetty
Owner/Operator: INEOS (acquired from BP in 2017)
Capacity: Nominal ~575,000–610,000 b/d; carries liquids from ~85 UK and Norwegian fields — roughly 40% of UK North Sea oil
Handles: Stabilised Forties Blend delivered at Hound Point (a Dated Brent benchmark grade); gas liquids to Grangemouth
Strategic role: The upstream leg of the Forties chain on this map — wellhead to Hound Point loading to Rotterdam; a single-system chokepoint for a large share of UK production
Risks: Single-system concentration — outages at Kinneil or on the main line ripple directly into the Dated Brent benchmark; ageing infrastructure; declining North Sea throughput</description>
