			<Folder>
				<name>Submarine / export sea-lines</name>
				<Placemark>
					<name>Ras Markaz SPM Twin Subsea Lines</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Route: The floating terminal ~7 km offshore → shore crossing → the Ras Markaz tank park; twin 42-inch pipelines, ~7 km at sea plus ~3.5 km on land
Owner/Operator: OTTCO (OQ group)
Handles: Crude in both directions by design — VLCC/ULCC discharges pumped ashore to the tanks today, with export loading capability built in; four main pumping stations drive the transfer
Strategic role: The umbilical of the whole Ras Markaz concept — the only physical link between the deep-draft mooring and the storage park
Risks: Twin-line concentration; open-coast subsea exposure; pumping-station dependence</description>
