			<Placemark>
				<name>Muscat–Sohar Product Pipeline (MSPP)</name>
				<description>Status: Operational
Route: Mina al-Fahal refinery → the Al Jifnain terminal (the distribution hub serving Muscat and its airport) → along the Batinah coast → Sohar refinery and port; ~290 km
Owner/Operator: OQ (with the Al Jifnain terminal as the central distribution node)
Handles: Gasoline, diesel and jet fuel between the country&apos;s two northern refineries; jet supply toward Muscat International Airport
Strategic role: Connects Oman&apos;s two refining centres into one products system and cut thousands of tanker-truck movements off the coastal highway
Risks: Single products corridor for the capital region; coastal infrastructure exposure</description>
