			<Placemark id="ADDRRB00000000000001">
				<name>Rostock–Böhlen product pipeline (RRB)</name>
				<description>Status: Operational
Route: Rostock oil port (GÖR terminal) → Leuna → Dow Böhlen cracker complex; ~430 km, up to 16-inch; in service since 1997
Owner/Operator: Dow Olefinverbund (Dow Chemical)
Handles: Naphtha, pyrolysis gasoline and condensate; also approved for pentane, benzene, crude (Rostock–Leuna) and C3+ LPG
Connectivity: Feeds the Böhlen naphtha cracker (ethylene and propylene for Schkopau and Leuna); part of Dow&apos;s ~1,300 km Central German network
Recent: Dow has applied to extend the approved cargo list to bio-based and recycled feedstocks (HVO-type and plastic-waste-derived)
Strategic role: The petrochemical twin of the Schwedt crude line — the second artery making Rostock the seaborne gateway for eastern Germany&apos;s refining and chemical industry
Risks: Single-line dependence for the Böhlen cracker&apos;s feedstock; cracker margin exposure</description>
