		<Folder>
			<name>Maritime Routes</name>
			<Folder>
				<name>Crude-grade delivery routes</name>
				<Placemark>
					<name>Cold Lake Blend route</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Crude: Cold Lake Blend
API: ~19.5–20°
Sulfur: ~3.5–3.9%
Type: Heavy, sour diluted bitumen
Origin: Cold Lake oil sands, Alberta — in-situ steam recovery, blended with diluent and moved toward Edmonton and the Trans Mountain system
Markets: Canada and the US; growing exports to the US West Coast and Asia via Westridge; Rotterdam is a representative route rather than the grade&apos;s primary destination
Used for: Heavy fuel components, asphalt feedstock and diesel in coker-equipped refineries
Pricing: Discount to WTI and Brent — density, sulphur and conversion costs; varies with pipeline space, freight and heavy-crude demand
Vessels: Aframax from Westridge; larger onward cargoes may need transshipment
Transit: ~30–40 days to Rotterdam via the Pacific, Panama, the Atlantic and the Channel
Risks: Pipeline congestion; diluent costs; Alberta wildfires; Vancouver loading limits; Panama delays; dense Channel traffic</description>
					<styleUrl>#msn_icon?color=1976d2&amp;id=2000&amp;scale=4010</styleUrl>
					<LineString>
