				<Placemark>
					<name>Azeri light route</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Crude: Azeri Light
API: ~35.3–35.6°
Sulfur: ~0.18–0.20%
Type: Light, sweet
Origin: Azeri–Chirag–Gunashli fields, offshore Azerbaijan — BTC pipeline to Ceyhan, Türkiye
Markets: Mediterranean and European refiners (France, Italy, Croatia, Netherlands)
Used for: Gasoline, naphtha, jet, diesel and petrochemical feedstocks
Pricing: Variable premium or discount to Dated Brent on Mediterranean demand, freight and availability
Vessels: Typically Aframax or Suezmax loaded at Ceyhan
Connectivity: Route to Cressier — Ceyhan → Fos-sur-Mer → SPSE → Jura line → Cressier (VAROPreem); alternatively by sea via Gibraltar and the Channel to Rotterdam
Transit: ~5–7 days to Fos-sur-Mer; ~12–16 days to Rotterdam
Risks: BTC outages; Ceyhan loading disruption; Turkish and Mediterranean geopolitics; Gibraltar and Channel congestion; crude-quality contamination</description>
					<styleUrl>#msn_ylw-pushpin1</styleUrl>
					<LineString>
						<tessellate>1</tessellate>
