				<Placemark>
					<name>Arab Light &amp; Arab Super Light route</name>
					<description><![CDATA[Status: Operational
Crude: Arab Light & Arab Super Light
API: 32–36° / >40°
Sulfur: 1.3–2.2% / <0.5%
Type: Medium sour / very light sweet
Origin: Saudi Arabia — exported through the Ras Tanura and Juaymah terminals
Markets: Mainly Asia; additional sales to NW Europe, the Mediterranean and the US
Used for: Arab Light covers the full product slate; Super Light is prized for naphtha, gasoline, LPG and petrochemical feedstocks
Pricing: Monthly Aramco OSPs — European cargoes vs ICE Brent, Asian cargoes vs Dubai/Oman
Vessels: Usually VLCC; Suezmax depending on cargo size and routing
Transit: ~25–35 days to Rotterdam via the Red Sea and Suez; longer around the Cape
Risks: Hormuz disruption; Red Sea and Bab el-Mandeb security; Suez congestion; war-risk premiums; Cape rerouting]]></description>
