			<Folder>
				<name>Gauge / reference points</name>
				<Placemark>
					<name>Kaub</name>
					<description>Status: Reduced
Operated by: German Federal Waterways and Shipping Administration (WSV)
Role: Reference gauge for Rhine navigation — the shallowest stretch of the Middle Rhine, between Mainz and Koblenz; the single reading fuel and freight markets watch to set barge loadings between ARA and southern Germany / Switzerland. Normal August level ~200 cm; below the ~78 cm equivalent most barges must lighten; around 40 cm shipping runs in emergency mode
Recent: All-time record low in August 2026 — ~21 cm on 3–4 Aug, ~16–17 cm on 10–11 Aug, below 10 cm on 14 Aug; forecast hovering near 20 cm before edging above 30 cm around 23 Aug
Strategic role: Where a weather event becomes a freight premium and an inland supply squeeze — the textbook case of a physical constraint setting prices
Risks: Third major low-water shock since 2018; heat and low soil moisture across southern Germany; recovery needs weeks of sustained rain</description>
