	<Folder>
		<name>D. Storage &amp; Pricing</name>
		<Folder>
			<name>Storage &amp; Depots</name>
			<Folder>
				<name>Crude Storage</name>
				<Placemark>
					<name>LOOP Clovelly Storage Hub</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Owner/Operator: LOOP LLC
Role: The onshore half of the LOOP system — crude storage in salt-dome caverns and tanks at Clovelly, buffering offshore tanker operations against pipeline schedules
Storage capacity: Tens of millions of barrels across eight caverns and surface tankage
Connectivity: Subsea pipeline from the marine terminal; LOCAP onward to St. James; Mars and other offshore Gulf grades also land in this system
Strategic role: The cavern buffer that makes VLCC economics work on the US Gulf — and a delivery point in the Gulf sour crude market alongside St. James
Risks: Hurricane corridor; cavern-integrity management; dependence on the single offshore terminal upstream</description>
					<styleUrl>#msn_red-circle11</styleUrl>
					<Point>
						<coordinates>-90.26957160699486,29.44742710537982,0</coordinates>
					</Point>
				</Placemark>
				<Placemark>
					<name>Enbridge Cushing Terminal</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Owner/Operator: Enbridge
Role: The largest single-operator position at the WTI delivery hub — ~20 million barrels of floating-roof crude tankage south of Cushing town
Storage capacity: ~20 million barrels within the hub&apos;s ~90 million total working capacity (~300 tanks)
Connectivity: Manifolded into the hub&apos;s inbound lines (Keystone, Basin, Flanagan South, White Cliffs) and outbound systems (Seaway, Marketlink, Ozark to Wood River)
Strategic role: Where a large share of the barrels that settle NYMEX WTI physically sit — the tanks behind the world&apos;s most-watched Wednesday inventory number
Risks: Basis blowouts when inbound exceeds outbound capacity (the April 2020 lesson); tornado alley weather; contract-storage cycle swings</description>
					<styleUrl>#default0</styleUrl>
					<Point>
						<coordinates>-96.75,35.94,0</coordinates>
					</Point>
				</Placemark>
				<Placemark>
					<name>Plains All American Cushing Terminal</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Owner/Operator: Plains All American Pipeline
Role: Co-largest tank farm at the hub — ~20 million barrels, tied into Plains&apos; Permian and Mid-Continent gathering systems
Storage capacity: ~20 million barrels of floating-roof tankage
Connectivity: Inbound from the Basin pipeline (Permian barrels) among others; outbound to the Gulf systems; Diamond pipeline (Plains–Valero JV, 200,000 b/d to the Memphis refinery) departs the hub
Strategic role: The Permian&apos;s traditional inland parking lot — Plains connects wellhead gathering in Texas to the paper market in Oklahoma
Risks: Storage-contract renewal cycles; the structural shift of Permian barrels flowing straight to Houston instead of via Cushing</description>
					<styleUrl>#default0</styleUrl>
					<Point>
						<coordinates>-96.72458171451837,35.95998675420457,0</coordinates>
					</Point>
				</Placemark>
				<Placemark>
					<name>Cushing Independent &amp; Midstream Terminals</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Owner/Operator: ONEOK (~7.8 million barrels, ex-Magellan), Energy Transfer (~7.6 million at the Rose Rock terminal), Enterprise Products (~3.1 million) and smaller operators
Role: The rest of the world&apos;s largest tank farm — the multi-operator tankage that makes Cushing storage a tradable service, not one company&apos;s asset
Storage capacity: ~20+ million barrels combined across the independent and midstream positions
Connectivity: Fully manifolded into the hub — any tank can in principle serve any pipeline, which is what makes WTI delivery frictionless
Strategic role: The competitive depth behind the benchmark — multiple operators quoting storage is why the delivery mechanism is trusted
Risks: Consolidation reducing operator diversity; ageing tankage; utilisation swings between contango and backwardation</description>
					<styleUrl>#default0</styleUrl>
					<Point>
						<coordinates>-96.75158953706269,36.00946085727618,0</coordinates>
					</Point>
				</Placemark>
			</Folder>
