				<Placemark id="08F5E005523EB856C896">
					<name>Vopak Terminal Vlaardingen</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Owner/Operator: Royal Vopak
Role: Independent liquid-bulk terminal in the Port of Rotterdam specialised in biofuels and specialty products — vegetable oils, animal fats, biodiesel, oleochemicals, base oils, sustainable feedstocks
Storage capacity: ~564,000–600,000 m³ in ~292 tanks (250–6,240 m³); 3 seagoing berths (max ~13 m draught), 10 barge berths, rail and road access
Recent: 16 new tanks (64,000 m³) commissioned in 2023 for waste-based feedstocks used in biodiesel, renewable diesel and SAF production
Strategic role: A major European hub for biofuel feedstocks within the ARA trading area — the storage side of the renewable-fuels chain
Risks: Fire and contamination; product-segregation requirements; Rhine and port logistics; dependence on European biofuel demand</description>
