				<Placemark id="06D7DDADB63F32DB299F">
					<name>Mont Belvieu, Texas</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Role: North America&apos;s largest NGL and LPG storage and fractionation hub — and the global pricing benchmark for propane and butane (&quot;Mt. Belvieu&quot;), as Henry Hub is for gas and Cushing for crude
Infrastructure: Massive underground salt-cavern storage in the Barbers Hill dome (propane, butane, ethane, iso-butane, natural gasoline, mixed Y-grade); large-scale fractionation plants; LPG export links to the Houston Ship Channel
Connectivity: Pipeline inflows from the Permian, Eagle Ford, Bakken and Marcellus; petrochemical feedstock distribution networks
Recent: US shale growth turned it from a regional LPG centre into the dominant export supply hub for propane and butane to Asia, Europe and Latin America
Strategic role: The central balancing point of US NGL production — spot prices, futures, swaps and international cargo pricing all key off Mont Belvieu assessments
Risks: Gulf hurricanes; fractionation and cavern outages; export-dock congestion</description>
