					<name>SKA Fuel Terminal</name>
					<description>Status: OperationalStatus: Operational
Owner/Operator: SKA International Group — independent fuel logistics operator
Role: Independent refined-products import and storage terminal in the Umm Qasr / Khor al-Zubair port zone — diesel, gasoline and jet fuel landed by tanker for distribution into southern Iraq
Connectivity: Truck loading into the Basra region; part of the private import infrastructure covering the products Iraq&apos;s refineries don&apos;t yet supply
Strategic role: A window into Iraq&apos;s paradox — OPEC&apos;s second crude producer importing its own road fuels through private coastal terminals
Risks: Import dependence on Gulf shipping; storage capacity and specifications to verify; congestion in the port zone</description>
