Role: Jordan&apos;s sole maritime energy gateway — crude and refined-product imports, LPG, and LNG via a floating import terminal
Connectivity: Onward largely by road toward the Zarqa refinery region and inland demand centres
Strategic role: Virtually all of Jordan&apos;s hydrocarbon imports enter through this short stretch of coast — the country&apos;s single energy artery
Risks: Same Bab el-Mandeb exposure as neighbouring Eilat (freight and insurance costs spiked in the Red Sea crisis); single-gateway dependence; limited storage depth</description>
