				<Placemark>
					<name>Gustavsburg/Raunheim fuel depots</name>
					<description>Status: Operational
Owner/Operator: Independent tank-storage operators; the airport-side kerosene lines are run by dedicated pipeline companies (Mainline, Dettmer — second Gustavsburg link opened 2012)
Role: Jet-fuel and products tank farms at the southern end of the RMR pipeline — the last storage step before Frankfurt Airport; also diesel, gasoline and heating oil for the Rhine-Main region
Connectivity: RMR southern branch (Udenheim fork); Kelsterbach river port on the Main for barge supply; the NATO pipeline also feeds the area; kerosene reaches the airport exclusively by pipeline — two lines from Gustavsburg, one from Raunheim, two from Kelsterbach
Recent: Frankfurt Airport stayed fully supplied through the 2018, 2022 and 2026 Rhine crises while barge-fed regions upstream saw shortages — the pipeline-protected side of the Kaub story
Strategic role: Where a national products pipeline turns into airport supply — Germany&apos;s largest hub is fuelled through these tanks
Risks: One airport&apos;s fuel supply concentrated on a few depots and pipes; RMR outage exposure; Main low water for the barge alternative</description>
