		<Folder>
			<name>Pricing Hubs</name>
			<Placemark>
				<name>ARA Pricing Hub (Amsterdam–Rotterdam–Antwerp)</name>
				<description>Status: Operational
Role: Europe&apos;s refined-products pricing hub — the zone whose barge deals set the continent&apos;s fuel prices
Benchmark instruments: Platts and Argus FOB ARA barge assessments (gasoline, diesel, jet, VLSFO); ICE Low Sulphur Gasoil futures, physically delivered inside this ring
Physical basis: The assets within this circle on the map — Port of Rotterdam, Port of Antwerp-Bruges, Port of Amsterdam, the Pernis refining cluster, Vopak Vlaardingen, Maasvlakte storage, Moerdijk and the RRP pipeline feeding the Rhine corridor
Relationship to Brent: ARA is the natural buyer of the Dated Brent (BFOET) basket loading at North Sea terminals like Hound Point — and since 2023, WTI Midland delivered CIF Rotterdam counts within Dated Brent itself
Recent: 2026 — the record Rhine low water decoupled inland prices from ARA quotes: barge freight, not product value, drove the spread upstream
Strategic role: Where European paper meets barges — the price the whole Rhine story keys off
Risks: Structural demand decline; refinery closures shrinking the physical base; low-water distortions</description>
