			<Placemark>
				<name>Cushing Pricing Hub (WTI delivery point)</name>
				<description>Status: Operational
Role: The settlement point of the world&apos;s most traded oil future — a landlocked Oklahoma tank-farm town, the &quot;pipeline crossroads of the world&quot;
Benchmark instruments: NYMEX/CME WTI Light Sweet crude futures, physically delivered in Cushing — the screen price the world calls &quot;WTI&quot;
Physical basis: ~90 million barrels of commercial tank capacity at the junction of inbound pipelines from the Permian, Rockies and Canada and outbound systems to the Gulf — the Seaway link toward Freeport and Texas City appears on this map
Recent: April 2020&apos;s negative prices were a Cushing event — futures holders facing delivery into brim-full tanks; the export era keeps pulling physical price discovery to the coast while the paper anchor stays here
Strategic role: The inland reference of the US price — its weekly storage number is a market signal in itself
Risks: Landlocked basis blowouts; relevance migration toward Houston; pipeline reversals rewriting its flows</description>
