			<Placemark>
				<name>US Gulf Coast Pricing Hub (Houston)</name>
				<description>Status: Operational
Role: The export-parity pricing hub of US crude and the products pricing centre of the Gulf Coast
Benchmark instruments: WTI Houston (MEH) and Platts AGS export-grade assessments; USGC products quotes; the marginal barrel the world buys is priced here
Physical basis: On this map — the Houston Ship Channel / Buffalo Bayou complex, Port of Texas City, Port Freeport, Mont Belvieu (the global NGL/LPG benchmark inside the same ring), with Corpus Christi down the coast and the Permian pipelines behind them
Recent: Since the 2015 export-ban lift, price discovery has shifted coastward; WTI Midland&apos;s inclusion in Dated Brent tied this shore directly to Europe&apos;s benchmark
Strategic role: Where American production meets world prices — the Cushing–Houston spread is pipeline economics made visible
Risks: Hurricanes; export-dock congestion; benchmark fragmentation across competing assessments</description>
