			<Placemark>
				<name>Singapore Pricing Hub (MOPS)</name>
				<description>Status: Operational
Role: Asia&apos;s products pricing hub — the proof that refining, storage, shipping and trading can make a benchmark without a single oil field
Benchmark instruments: MOPS (Mean of Platts Singapore) assessments — gasoline 92/95/97, jet, 10ppm gasoil, VLSFO and HSFO, naphtha; the world&apos;s reference bunker prices; even the Dubai crude benchmark is assessed during the Singapore trading window
Physical basis: On this map — Singapore–Jurong Island, the ExxonMobil Jurong and Aster Bukom refineries, Pulau Bukom terminal, the independent tank farms and the bunkering anchorages, with Malacca at the doorstep
Recent: 2026 — record strait traffic and Hormuz-rerouted flows reinforced its role as Asia&apos;s clearing house
Strategic role: The price every Asian fuel contract references — formed where the flows squeeze past
Risks: Malacca disruption; competition from Chinese pricing ambitions; a thinning local refining base</description>
