			<Placemark>
				<name>Fujairah &amp; Gulf of Oman Pricing Hub</name>
				<description>Status: Operational
Role: The East-of-Suez crude and bunkering pricing zone — outside the strait, which 2026 turned from convenience into consecration
Benchmark instruments: IFAD Murban futures, physically delivered at Fujairah; the FOIZ weekly inventory data — the Gulf&apos;s stock signal; Platts Fujairah bunker assessments; the DME Oman contract delivers FOB Mina al-Fahal down this coast (on this map), completing the eastern benchmark trio with the Dubai assessment
Physical basis: Port of Fujairah, the ADCOP pipeline terminus, the FOIZ tank farms and the bunkering anchorage — with the Omani system southward
Recent: 2026 — the working price point of a closed-strait world: bunker demand, storage value and Murban&apos;s non-Hormuz delivery all gained weight
Strategic role: Where the Gulf&apos;s oil gets priced when the Gulf itself is shut
Risks: Tanker incidents (2019 precedent); anchorage congestion; dependence on ADCOP throughput</description>
