			<Placemark>
				<name>Mediterranean Pricing Hub (Augusta, Sicily)</name>
				<description>Status: Operational
Role: The Mediterranean&apos;s traditional cargo-pricing anchor — and this map&apos;s example of a hub outliving its benchmark
Benchmark instruments: CIF Augusta was the basis of the Urals Mediterranean quote for decades; Mediterranean assessments for CPC Blend, Libyan, Caspian and Saharan grades still reference the Sicily delivery zone as differentials to Dated Brent
Physical basis: The Augusta refinery (Sonatrach), the giant ISAB Priolo complex next door, the Santa Panagia terminals and storage — central Mediterranean geography between Suez, Gibraltar and the Adriatic
Recent: The 2022–23 embargo killed the Urals CIF Augusta trade that made the location famous; ISAB&apos;s forced sale from Lukoil scrambled its anchor tenant; Med pricing increasingly leans on other baskets
Strategic role: Still the reference point for cross-Med cargoes — and the demonstration that a benchmark can die while its infrastructure remains
Risks: Sicilian refining rationalisation; benchmark migration; the hub&apos;s fate if ISAB closes</description>
