					<Point>
						<gx:drawOrder>1</gx:drawOrder>
						<coordinates>7.002894992897522,50.8164512557096,0</coordinates>
					</Point>
				</Placemark>
				<Placemark>
					<name>BASF Ludwigshafen</name>
					<visibility>0</visibility>
					<description>Status: Operational
Owner/Operator: BASF SE (headquarters on site)
Configuration: The world&apos;s largest integrated chemical complex (Verbund) — two steam crackers and several hundred interconnected plants on ~10 km², each unit feeding the next with by-products and heat; supplied by naphtha, LPG and natural gas
Main products: Ethylene, propylene and the full downstream chain — plastics, plasticisers, coatings, agro and pharma intermediates, ammonia, fertilisers
Connectivity: Rhine barge harbour; southern terminus of the RMR products pipeline (connected at Oppau); MIDAL gas pipeline; dense rail; river water for cooling
Recent: August 2026 — force majeure declared on DINP and DPHP plasticisers citing extreme weather and severe Rhine logistics constraints, with a switch to shallow-draft vessels; 2018 and 2022 low water also forced output cuts
Strategic role: The demand anchor of the Rhine chemical corridor — pipeline-protected for products (RMR) yet river-dependent for cooling and feedstock logistics
Risks: Rhine low water (cooling and barges); European gas and energy costs; deep plant-network interdependence</description>
