				<Placemark id="00C02568723EB7B9A5C6">
					<name>MOL Petrochemicals Tiszaújváros</name>
					<visibility>0</visibility>
					<description>Status: Operational
Owner/Operator: MOL Petrochemicals (MOL Group); the synthetic-rubber unit is a JV with Japan&apos;s ENEOS
Configuration: Two steam crackers (~660,000 t/yr ethylene, ~130,000 t/yr butadiene), five polymer units (~765,000 t/yr PE+PP), a 200,000 t/yr polyether-polyol complex, and an SSBR rubber unit; a 100,000 t/yr propylene (OCT) unit due on stream in 2026 after delays
Main feedstocks: Naphtha and LPG piped from MOL&apos;s Duna refinery and Slovnaft Bratislava, plus imports; first ISCC PLUS-certified circular feedstock processed September 2025
Main products: Olefins, HDPE, LDPE, PP, polyether polyols, propylene glycol, hydrogen peroxide, solution SBR
Markets: Hungary and Central Europe
Strategic role: The petrochemical arm of the MOL system — the downstream customer of the Duna and Bratislava refineries on this map
Risks: Feedstock dependence on two refineries (and thus on their crude supply); European petrochemical margins; project delays</description>
