				<Placemark id="0C008C1AB53EB8584258">
					<name>Dow Terneuzen</name>
					<visibility>0</visibility>
					<description>Status: Operational
Owner/Operator: Dow Benelux (Dow Inc.)
Configuration: Three steam crackers (LHC1–3) — ~1.8 Mt/yr ethylene, ~900,000 t/yr propylene, 240,000 t/yr butadiene, 900,000 t/yr aromatics; 16 plants and ~800 products, with Trinseo and Olin co-located
Main feedstocks: Naphtha and LPG in roughly equal shares by pipeline from Rotterdam and Antwerp, plus ship and rail; small volumes of bio-naphtha and pyrolysis oil
Markets: NW European converter and specialty-chemicals industry
Recent: The 600,000 t/yr LHC3 cracker was idled from June 2025 on weak European demand and restarted in June 2026 as polyethylene and polyurethane chains tightened
Strategic role: The Netherlands&apos; largest cracker site — the Scheldt-side counterpart of the Antwerp cluster
Risks: European demand weakness; energy costs; cracker overcapacity; single-site concentration for Dow in Europe</description>
