				<Placemark id="05EE12FD073EB86434EF">
					<name>BASF Antwerp</name>
					<visibility>0</visibility>
					<description>Status: Operational
Owner/Operator: BASF Antwerpen (BASF SE)
Configuration: ~50 plants in ~15 integrated value chains on ~6 km² — the Verbund model; steam cracker of ~1.1 Mt/yr ethylene plus propylene and C4s; ethylene-oxide capacity expanded by ~400,000 t/yr in 2023
Main feedstocks: Naphtha and LPG sourced globally by ship, plus natural gas; some pyrolysis-oil co-processing
Main products: Olefins, ethylene oxide and glycols, acrylic acid and superabsorbents, amines, aniline, caprolactam, MDI, surfactants
Recent: October 2025 — structural cost-cutting target raised from €100m to €150m by end-2028, with ~600 job cuts (about one position in six)
Strategic role: Europe&apos;s second-largest chemical complex, inside the Antwerp port cluster
Risks: European energy costs; demand weakness; restructuring execution; port and Scheldt dependence</description>
