				<Placemark id="0467A13A993EB8752C2C">
					<name>INEOS Antwerp</name>
					<visibility>0</visibility>
					<description>Status: Operational
Owner/Operator: INEOS — Oxide at Zwijndrecht, Phenol at Doel, Olefins Belgium for Project ONE at Lillo/Zandvliet
Configuration: INEOS Phenol ~680,000 t/yr (historically the world&apos;s largest single phenol plant) with co-product acetone; INEOS Oxide ethylene oxide and derivatives plus ENB and its own CHP plant; Project ONE under construction — a 1.45 Mt/yr ethane cracker plus a propane-dehydrogenation unit
Main feedstocks: Imported US ethane by dedicated gas carriers for Project ONE; propane for the PDH; benzene, propylene and ethylene by pipeline and the deep-sea ethylene terminal
Markets: European polymers, engineering plastics, coatings, surfactants, pharma intermediates
Strategic role: Europe&apos;s biggest cracker investment in a generation — betting US ethane economics against naphtha-based rivals
Risks: Project ONE execution and its permitting history; ethane freight exposure; European demand; energy costs</description>
