				<Placemark>
					<name>RAPID Petrochemical Complex</name>
					<visibility>0</visibility>
					<description>Status: Operational
Owner/Operator: PRefChem (Petronas) for the cracker; downstream JVs with LyondellBasell, BASF, Evonik, Itochu and PTT Global Chemical
Configuration: Mixed-feed steam cracker of ~3 Mt/yr olefins feeding ~4.5 Mt/yr of petrochemicals — 900,000 t/yr PP, PE lines, MEG, isononanol, 1-butene, hydrogen peroxide; 1.22 GW cogeneration and air-separation units on site
Main feedstocks: Naphtha and refinery streams from the RAPID refinery next door, plus imported LPG and ethane-range feed
Markets: Malaysia, SE Asia and export
Strategic role: The petrochemical half of Pengerang — integrated with the 300,000 b/d refinery inside one 2,000-hectare footprint, competing with Singapore&apos;s Jurong hub
Risks: Shared-site exposure to refinery outages; Asian petrochemical overcapacity; margin weakness</description>
