				<Placemark>
					<name>Stenungsund petrochemical cluster</name>
					<visibility>0</visibility>
					<description>Status: Operational
Owner/Operator: Borealis (cracker + polyethylene, majority OMV), INEOS Inovyn (PVC, caustic soda), Perstorp (specialities + Scandinavia&apos;s largest RME biodiesel plant), Nouryon; ~2,500 direct jobs
Role: Sweden&apos;s largest chemical cluster and its only steam-cracker site
Main feedstocks: Naphtha and LPG delivered by sea; growing share of renewable and recycled feeds
Main products: Ethylene, propylene, polyethylene (incl. cable-grade XLPE), PVC, speciality chemicals, RME biodiesel
Recent: Borealis cracker revamp completed, XLPE expansion by 2027; ~SEK 10bn cluster decarbonisation plan (−1 Mt CO₂/yr); Project Air renewable methanol
Strategic role: The main light-feedstock customer on Sweden&apos;s west coast, sitting between the Lysekil and Gothenburg refineries
Risks: Naphtha/LPG price exposure; energy costs vs US and Middle East crackers; one cracker for the whole country</description>
