				<Placemark>
					<name>Lülsdorf chemical site</name>
					<visibility>0</visibility>
					<description>Status: Operational
Owner/Operator: International Chemical Investors Group (ICIG) since June 2023, ex-Evonik; KFS Biodiesel operates the on-site biodiesel unit; 600+ employees
Main products: Cyanuric chloride (crop-protection intermediates), potassium derivatives, sodium/potassium alkoxides — the transesterification catalysts of the biodiesel industry, produced exclusively for Evonik until 2027; FAME biodiesel
Connectivity: Rhine barge access on the right bank, opposite Wesseling; road and rail
Recent: Divested by Evonik in 2023 as the first step of its Performance Materials exit; ICIG committed to invest, with no operational redundancies until 2032
Strategic role: The right-bank half of the Wesseling cluster — and a quiet link between Rhine chemistry and the biodiesel value chain
Risks: Rhine dependence; ownership transition; niche-product demand</description>
